#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""mesh-novelty — a Shannon-surprise signal over the mesh's own event stream.

Well-studied field: information theory. The self-information of an event is
I(x) = -log2 P(x): rare/new events carry many bits, routine events carry few.
The mesh emits hundreds of routine lines ([done], [taking], [git-lock]) and a
handful of rare ones ([gap], [incident], [health-fail], a never-seen tag, a
first-seen device). Without a measure, the operator drowns in noise and the
mesh wakes expensive minds for nothing.

mesh-novelty reads the board (and presence), learns the BASELINE distribution
of event types, and scores a RECENT window:
  - per-event surprisal under the baseline (add-1 smoothed; a NEW type = max bits)
  - an aggregate novelty score (mean bits of the window)
  - the specific high-surprise events + first-seen entities (devices/tools/errors)

Why it matters (two payoffs, both real):
  1. LEGIBILITY — after an absence, "what was genuinely NEW vs routine" in one
     line, so the digest surfaces signal not 200 lines of noise.
  2. SPEND — a cheap reflex can gate expensive minds: wake on HIGH novelty,
     stay silent on routine. (Attention follows information, not volume.)

  mesh-novelty                 report novelty of the recent window vs baseline
  mesh-novelty --window N      recent window = N board lines (default 40)
  mesh-novelty --threshold B   stream mode: print a feed line only if score >= B bits
  mesh-novelty --edge          edge-triggered: emit only on mean shift >±0.5b or new top-5
  mesh-novelty --edge --min-gap S  + a min-interval floor: hold a real edge if the last
                               emit was < S sec ago (the change still fires once S elapses)
  mesh-novelty --conditional   (alias --ctx) score CONTEXTUAL prediction error, not marginal
                               rarity — combines with the report / --threshold / --edge
  mesh-novelty --diversity     Shannon-evenness of the BASELINE type distribution's SHAPE
                               (not per-event surprisal — see DIVERSITY section below)
  mesh-novelty --levels        LOCAL-GLOBAL two-timescale deviance (report-only; --json for the
                               dict) — classify each recent event as REGIME-ONSET/LOCAL-BLIP/etc
  mesh-novelty --territory     DETERRITORIALIZATION COEFFICIENT (report-only; --json) — split the
                               window early/late and classify each surprising surge as RELATIVE
                               (recaptured — snaps back) vs ABSOLUTE (a line of flight — not recaptured)
  mesh-novelty --bayesian      BAYESIAN SURPRISE (Itti & Baldi; report-only; --json; alias --wow) — score
                               each recent type by how much it MOVES the belief (KL of the Dirichlet
                               update), not how improbable it is; flags HABITUATED types (high Shannon,
                               ~zero belief-move — a wake raw surprisal over-pays every recurrence) vs
                               genuinely MODEL-MOVING ones. Attention follows belief-update, not rarity.
  mesh-novelty --valence       ENACTIVE VALENCE (report-only; --json) — significance = a viability-
                               relevant event's valence × the mesh's CURRENT fused posture
                               (.situation.state NOMINAL/WATCH/ALERT). The one axis that reads the
                               mesh's own body-state, not the board: the SAME [gap]/[health-fail]
                               compounds when the node is already ALERT (attention follows viability,
                               not information). Missing/stale posture → UNKNOWN, state-neutral.
  mesh-novelty --progress      COMPRESSION PROGRESS / STAGNATION LENGTH (Herrmann & Schmidhuber 2026;
                               report-only; --json) — interestingness is a DERIVATIVE (is the board's own
                               symbol SEQUENCE still getting more compressible?), NOT a level of surprise.
                               The Noisy-TV guard: a churn of first-seen types MAXIMIZES surprisal AND
                               --bayesian belief-move yet has ZERO compression progress → LEARNING vs
                               NOISE vs MASTERED. Embodies the HELD fix at :425-459.
  mesh-novelty --tempering     COGNITIVE TEMPERING (report-only; --json) — the focusing↔diversifying
                               opponent pair (Vervaeke's THIRD RR opponent, distinct from
                               explore↔exploit and efficiency↔resiliency), read as activity-evenness
                               (Pielou J: low=FOCUSED/concentrated, high=DIFFUSE/spread) COUPLED to
                               arousal (.situation.state). RR-correct is an arousal-tracking EDGE, not
                               a fixed midpoint: FOCUS under ALERT is right (narrow to the threat);
                               FOCUS under NOMINAL is FIXATION (narrowed with no arousal to justify it).
  mesh-novelty --when          "WHEN"-EXPECTATION / TIME-LOCKED omission PE (Yaron/Shiramatsu/Takahashi/
                               Chao 2026; report-only; --json) — the omission axis in the default report
                               scores a type's SILENCE against its RATE over a count window (a memoryless
                               Bernoulli model). This one learns the type's ARRIVAL-INTERVAL law from the
                               board's own timestamps (regularity CV → REGULAR/POISSON/BURSTY) and scores
                               silence against how OVERDUE it is, capped at what the sample can resolve.
                               Reports where the two disagree: UNDER-CALLED / OVER-CALLED / UNDERPOWERED.
  mesh-novelty --features      FEATURE-SPECIFIC PREDICTION ERROR (Richter/Uran/Vinck/de Lange,
                               Imaging Neuroscience 2025-12-18; report-only; --json) — surprise has a
                               LEVEL, not just a magnitude: "a stimulus may be both predicted and
                               surprising, depending on the specific features". Every other mode here
                               scores ONE alphabet (event_type() = the bracket marker = the LOW,
                               surface feature). This one decomposes each event into form/actor/role
                               (role = the board grammar mesh-promises parses; the COARSE level) and
                               reports where the levels DISAGREE. On this board they are
                               anti-correlated (r(form,role) ≈ −0.41) and a low gate shares 1/60 of
                               its top decile with a high one — the scalar wakes on drops of rain.
  mesh-novelty --uncertainty   PREDICTION UNCERTAINTY as a SECOND, PROACTIVE boundary signal
                               (Nguyen/Etzel/Bezdek/Zacks, eLife 2026-07-07; report-only; --json) —
                               every other mode here scores an event that ALREADY ARRIVED (the
                               residual). This one scores the SPREAD of the model's own next-step
                               distribution, a property of the CONTEXT, computable BEFORE the next
                               line is posted. A context whose successor distribution has gone flat
                               emits no surprising line at all — each successor is individually
                               ordinary — so it is an event boundary the error axis cannot represent
                               at any threshold. Classifies the window ERROR-DRIVEN / UNCERTAINTY-
                               DRIVEN / BOTH, refuses NO-MODEL and UNDERPOWERED rows, and prints a
                               verdict about the NEXT, unposted line.
  mesh-novelty --test          smoke test

DIVERSITY (LITERATURE, live review 2026-07-02: biosemiotics — sign and meaning in living
systems, angle=a concrete METRIC this area uses to measure itself). Everything above scores
an INDIVIDUAL event against the baseline. It never asks a different, biosemiotically-real
question: does the baseline's own type-frequency distribution have the SHAPE of a working
sign repertoire at all? Zoosemiotic/bioacoustic work quantifies this: real communication
repertoires (animal call types, word frequencies) follow a Zipfian rank-frequency skew — a
few common signs, many rare ones — and Shannon entropy of the repertoire is used as a
ROBUST estimator of that skew because direct log-log slope-fitting is unreliable on the
small sample sizes typical of both animal-call corpora and (here) a ~40-line window
(Kershenbaum et al., "Shannon entropy as a robust estimator of Zipf's Law in animal vocal
communication repertoires", Methods in Ecology and Evolution 2021, 10.1111/2041-210X.13536;
recent grounding: "Linguistic laws in biology", arXiv:2310.07387; "For a semiotic of opacity:
the role of biosemiotics between AI and animal communication", 2025, applying this exact
skew-vs-uniform lens to critique AI animal-communication decoders). The counterintuitive
operational reading: a Zipfian code is markedly UNEVEN by construction (dominant + long
tail), so an event-type distribution trending toward UNIFORM (every marker equally likely)
is the anomaly, not the healthy state — the mesh's board vocabulary ([done]/[idle] common,
[incident]/[gap] rare) is expected to sit LOW-TO-MID on the evenness scale; a spike toward
BOTH extremes is diagnostic: near-0 evenness (an existing memory: [[operator-msg-board-broadcast-floods-responders]],
verbose-idle/phantom-taking floods) means the marker vocabulary has collapsed to a
monoculture, and near-1 evenness means posts are firing with no differentiated code at all
(pure noise, not a working repertoire). `diversity()` below reuses the SAME `base` Counter
`analyse()` already builds (no new data collection) — distinct from mean_bits (an event's
individual surprise) and from the eigenform/volatility/noisy-TV HELD blocks in analyse()
(those score dynamics of INDIVIDUAL scores over time; this scores the STATIC shape of the
distribution those scores are drawn from). Shipped as an opt-in `--diversity` flag, NOT
folded into the default `fmt()` text several tools already grep
([[cross-sense-vocab-contract]]: changing default sense output silently breaks consumers).

PREDICTIVE-CODING UPGRADE (live review 2026-06-20: predictive processing & the Bayesian brain
— a foundational idea we applied TOO LOOSELY). Predictive coding does NOT measure surprise as a
signal's marginal rarity; it transmits only the RESIDUAL against a CONTEXTUAL forward prediction
("explaining away" / repetition suppression — Millidge et al., "Predictive Coding: A Theoretical
and Experimental Review", arXiv:2107.12979; "Repetition suppression and its contextual determinants
in predictive coding", Cortex 2016; current framing: "The Information-Theoretic Imperative",
arXiv:2510.25883, 2025 — "transmit what is surprising rather than what is predicted"). The DEFAULT
score above is MARGINAL surprisal -log P(eᵢ): a [done] that ALWAYS follows [taking] (perfectly
predictable, ~0 true prediction error) scores identically to a [done] arriving with NO preceding
[taking] (genuinely unpredicted). That conflates rarity with surprise. --conditional scores the
predictive-coding quantity -log P(eᵢ | eᵢ₋₁) via a first-order Markov forward model over the
baseline: a predictable sequence is "explained away" (low bits → don't wake minds), a contextually
UNexpected transition scores high (wake). Default stays marginal (back-compat); consumers opt in.
This is distinct from PRECISION-weighting (scripts/mesh-precision, landed 2026-06-20) — that
weights HOW reliable a signal is; this measures WHETHER a signal was predicted from context.
"""
# ── review-fep-dark-room-prior-preference-2026-07-27 (LIVE literature — a CRITIQUE / failure mode) ──
# TASK: FEP / Active Inference (Friston) from the angle of a known CRITIQUE. The mesh has already landed
# the major critiques — the Emperor's-New-Markov-Blankets / Pearl-vs-Friston reification (mesh-perimeter),
# the small-world / frame-problem limit of relevance-realization (mesh-precision: Jaeger 2024,
# Parvizi-Wayne 2025), and the NOISY-TV / curiosity-trap (this file, 2026-06-21). The one canonical FEP
# failure mode NOT yet embodied is its most-cited: the DARK-ROOM PROBLEM.
#
# THE FAILURE MODE — the DARK ROOM. If a system minimises SURPRISE, why not seek the most predictable
# environment possible — a dark, silent, unchanging room — and stay there? A pure surprise-minimiser
# prefers predictable input, so it goes BLIND to a condition once that condition becomes predictable.
# This file IS a surprise-minimiser used as a SPEND gate ("wake on HIGH novelty, stay silent on
# routine"), and its own analyse() header already documents the dark-room in local form — the
# boiling-frog / eigenform ABSORPTION note: a persistent [health-fail]/[incident] recurs, accretes into
# `base`, its p(t) rises, its surprisal -log P FALLS, and it STOPS waking minds exactly because it is now
# chronic. That HELD fix was blocked because "a real regime change looks identical to a pathological
# accretion — separating them needs a reference the loop does NOT author."
#
# THE MECHANISM (the FEP's OWN resolution to the dark room) — PRIOR PREFERENCES. The FEP answer is that
# agents do not minimise raw surprise; they minimise surprise relative to PREFERRED observations (goal
# priors / the "C" vector) — outcomes they act to obtain (and to keep observing) even when unsurprising.
# Those preferences are DESIGN-SPECIFIED, not learned from the agent's own sensory history — which is
# precisely the "reference the loop does not author" the HELD note needed. So prior preferences unblock
# the absorption failure for the critical SUBSET (a curated must-attend tag set), while the GENERAL
# regime-change-vs-accretion problem stays correctly HELD (this does not touch it).
#   LIVE SOURCES (read 2026-07-27, current lit — not a fixed list):
#     • Karl Friston, Christopher Thornton, Andy Clark, "Free-energy minimization and the dark-room
#       problem", Frontiers in Psychology 3:130 (2012) — the canonical statement + the prior-preference
#       resolution. https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2012.00130
#     • Filippo Torresan, Ryota Kanai, Manuel Baltieri, "Prior preferences in active inference agents:
#       soft, hard, and goal shaping", arXiv:2512.03293 (Dec 2025) — the CURRENT treatment of HOW to
#       specify these preferences: hard (sharp) priors are brittle, soft/shaped priors are robust.
#       (The mesh already has the "by-name poke must-answer" floor on the room organ — same principle,
#       different organ; this extends the must-attend floor to the novelty spend-gate.)
#
# THE ONE CONCRETE APPLICATION (this edit): a PRIOR-PREFERENCE FLOOR. A design-specified must-attend tag
# set (MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_TAGS, default `incident health-fail gap`) is surfaced by analyse() as `pref_hits`
# WHATEVER its surprisal, shown by fmt() even on a "routine" window, and fires the --threshold wake gate
# regardless of mean_bits — deduped by TIME (re-assert every MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_REFRESH, default 1h) so a
# chronic critical condition is never permanently absorbed nor spammed each cron. The surprise MEASUREMENT
# is left PURE (mean_bits/scored untouched — no silent inflation); the floor is a parallel, labelled
# attend-regardless channel. RED-first test: a chronic [health-fail] absorbed to <4b still lands in
# pref_hits; MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_TAGS="" empties the set and the assertion goes red.
import sys, os, re, math, time, zlib, random, calendar
from collections import Counter, defaultdict

MESH = os.path.expanduser("~/.mesh")
CHAT = os.path.join(MESH, "chat.log")
PRESENCE = os.path.join(MESH, "presence.log")

TAG = re.compile(r'\[([a-z][a-z-]*)\]')
MAC = re.compile(r'\b([0-9A-Fa-f]{2}(?::[0-9A-Fa-f]{2}){5})\b')

BOARD = re.compile(r'^\d{2,4}[-:0-9T]*Z?\s+\S+\s+::')   # a real dated board line

# ── PRIOR-PREFERENCE FLOOR (active-inference dark-room fix) — see the header review block ──────────
# A DESIGN-SPECIFIED (not board-learned) set of must-attend tags: a preferred/critical observation the
# mind attends REGARDLESS of surprise. Because the set is not harvested from the board's own history, it
# CANNOT be absorbed into the baseline the way the boiling-frog / eigenform HELD note in analyse()
# describes — that is exactly why it unblocks the absorption failure for this critical subset.
PREF_TAGS = set(t for t in os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_TAGS", "incident health-fail gap").split() if t)
PREF_REFRESH = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_REFRESH", "3600"))  # re-assert cadence (s): a chronic
                                                                         # must-attend re-fires every hour,
                                                                         # never once-then-silent, never spam

# ── LOCAL–GLOBAL TWO-TIMESCALE DEVIANCE (predictive-processing local-global paradigm) ──────────────
# LITERATURE (live review 2026-07-27, angle = a concrete EXPERIMENT this area measures itself with):
# the LOCAL-GLOBAL oddball paradigm (Bekinschtein, Dehaene, Rohaut, Tadel, Cohen, Naccache, "Neural
# signature of the conscious processing of auditory regularities", PNAS 106:1672, 2009) — still the
# 2024-2025 workhorse for dissociating hierarchical levels of prediction error: a stimulus can be a
# LOCAL deviant (violates the last few items, short timescale, ~150 ms, automatic/feedforward,
# attention-independent) while being a GLOBAL standard (conforms to the block's established long-range
# rule, ~seconds, attention-dependent, top-down) — and vice-versa. The two dissociate in cortical
# locus, latency and consciousness-sensitivity. CURRENT: Jamali et al., "Parallel mechanisms signal a
# hierarchy of sequence structure violations in the auditory cortex", eLife 2025 (10.7554/eLife.102702)
# — local & global violations are signalled by PARALLEL, separable mechanisms, not one cascade; and
# "Localizing hierarchical prediction errors and precisions during an oddball task with volatility",
# Imaging Neuroscience 2025 (10.1162/imag_a_00461). THE GAP: this reflex scores every recent event's
# surprisal against ONE baseline (the long history `base`). It cannot dissociate a LOCAL-deviant-but-
# GLOBAL-standard blip (a routine type merely absent from the immediate context, then reappearing —
# the automatic local oddball, low wake value) from a LOCAL-standard-but-GLOBAL-deviant REGIME ONSET
# (a type rare in long history yet ALREADY RECURRING in the immediate window — an anomaly forming). The
# regime-onset case is the eigenform-absorption HELD block's COMPLEMENT caught at ONSET: eigenform flags
# the accretion AFTER the baseline has absorbed it (frequency rising across baselines, marginal surprise
# fallen); this flags it WHILE still global-rare but already local-recurring — i.e. before absorption.
# Report-only (does NOT touch the wake gate — the SPEND wiring stays the steward's, like the sibling
# HELD fixes); distinct from HGF-volatility (scales the bar by change-RATE) and the prior-preference
# floor (a design-fixed must-attend tag set). Two nested baselines: GLOBAL = long history `base`;
# LOCAL = the recent window minus its tip (the immediate short-timescale context).
LEVELS_TIP = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_LEVELS_TIP", "5"))     # # of most-recent events classified
LEVELS_HI  = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_LEVELS_HI", "4.0"))  # deviance bar (bits) — reuses the surprise bar

# ── DETERRITORIALIZATION COEFFICIENT: RELATIVE (recaptured) vs ABSOLUTE (line of flight) ────────────
# LITERATURE (live review 2026-07-28 — Deleuze & Guattari, assemblage/rhizome/machinic, angle = a
# concrete MEASURE the field uses on itself; doc: docs/reviews/deleuze-deterritorialization-coefficient-
# relative-vs-absolute-recapture-2026-07-28.md). D&G is a well-worked mesh seam (rhizome→mesh-sensor-tape,
# territorialization/DeLanda→mesh-digest, refrain→mesh-reflex-health, order-word→board, smooth/striated
# →velocity+distance, disjunctive-synthesis→mesh-situation). The one axis NOT embodied is the field's own
# MEASURE of a movement: the COEFFICIENT of deterritorialization, and its RELATIVE-vs-ABSOLUTE cut.
#
# THE MEASURE — every deterritorialization (an element ESCAPING its coded territory) has a coupled
# RETERRITORIALIZING edge, and the two uses are distinguished by RECAPTURE (Thornton, "On Lines of Flight",
# RHUL PhD 2018, pp.196-197, reading ATP 359 & 62): a RELATIVE (negative) deterritorialization is one where
# the assemblage "only changes in relation to a given form of stability that it maintains over time" — the
# escape is RECAPTURED, it snaps back; an ABSOLUTE (positive) deterritorialization — a LINE OF FLIGHT — is
# one where "one leaves all assemblages behind... entering another plane", the prior organisation is
# destroyed and NOT recaptured (ATP: relative D. is "stratic or interstratic", absolute D. "concern[s] the
# plane of consistency and its destratification"). So a surge is a line of flight ONLY if it is not pulled
# back — magnitude alone (a big surprise) does not tell you which; PERSISTENCE-past-the-reterritorializing-
# edge does. Guattari names the measurable form directly — the "coefficient of transversality", a group's
# tunable degree of openness-to-escape (Guattari, "Transversality", 1964 / Psychoanalysis & Transversality).
#
# THE GAP THIS NAMES — every axis on this file scores a surge's MAGNITUDE or its timescale at ONE moment:
# marginal surprisal (rarity NOW), --conditional (contextual residual NOW), --levels (short-vs-long deviance
# NOW). NONE asks the D&G question: did the surge STAY, or did the board's distribution RETERRITORIALIZE back
# to its prior shape? A one-shot spike that snaps back (a flapping sense, a burst that self-resolves) is a
# RELATIVE deterritorialization — low wake value — yet it reads MAX bits and (use-case-2) can wake a mind.
# The recapture read distinguishes it from an ABSOLUTE line of flight (a genuine new regime the board did
# NOT return from). DISTINCT from the two HELD blocks in analyse(): eigenform-absorption is the SAME type's
# surprise FALLING as it accretes across baselines (a false negative, needs a reference the loop can't
# author); this is the COMPLEMENT that IS self-authored — the reference is simply TIME-FORWARD recapture,
# observable on the board with a lag, no oracle. It does not judge whether an absolute shift is GOOD (that
# stays the steward's, like the siblings); it only measures relative-vs-absolute. Report-only, opt-in
# --territory; does NOT touch the wake gate (instrument-first, same discipline as --levels/--diversity).
ESCAPE_MIN = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_ESCAPE_MIN", "0.1"))  # min early-half freq-gain over baseline
BAYES_FRAC = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_BAYES_FRAC", "0.5"))   # frac of a NEW type's belief-move to call MODEL-MOVING
OMIT_MINEXP = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_OMIT_MINEXP", "1.0"))  # min EXPECTED occurrences for a type's SILENCE to count as an omission
# "WHEN"-EXPECTATION (--when; see the when_expectation() header block)
WHEN_MINIV   = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_WHEN_MINIV", "6"))        # min inter-arrival INTERVALS before a "when" law may be fitted
WHEN_CVFLOOR = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_WHEN_CVFLOOR", "0.05")) # CV clamp — a perfectly-regular sample would give an infinite Gamma shape
WHEN_KMAX    = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_WHEN_KMAX", "200.0"))   # Gamma shape ceiling (numeric guard on the same degeneracy)
WHEN_REG_CV  = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_WHEN_REG_CV", "0.5"))   # CV below which arrivals read REGULAR (sub-Poisson)
WHEN_BURST_CV= float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_WHEN_BURST_CV", "1.5")) # CV above which arrivals read BURSTY (super-Poisson / clustered)
                                                                     # to count as a deterritorializing surge
# COMPRESSION PROGRESS / STAGNATION LENGTH (--progress; see the function docstring)
PROGRESS_EPS    = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_PROGRESS_EPS", "0.02"))  # min amortized bits/symbol DROP to count as a compression breakthrough
PROGRESS_NSEG   = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_PROGRESS_NSEG", "12"))     # # of prefix checkpoints along the stagnation curve
PROGRESS_RHO_HI = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_PROGRESS_RHO", "0.7"))   # compressibility (out/in bytes) above which a STAGNATED stream reads as NOISE not MASTERED
PROGRESS_MIN    = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_PROGRESS_MIN", "40"))      # min symbols before a progress verdict is meaningful

# ── ENACTIVE VALENCE: viability-relative significance, STATE-DEPENDENT (report-only) ────────────────
# LITERATURE (live review 2026-07-30 — enactivism & 4E cognition, angle = an OPERATIONAL mechanism it
# proposes; doc: docs/reviews/enactivism-4e-enactive-valence-state-dependent-novelty-2026-07-30.md).
# Every axis on this file — marginal surprisal, --conditional, --bayesian, --levels, --territory,
# --diversity, omission, even the prior-preference dark-room floor — scores an event from the BOARD
# ALONE: an agent-INDEPENDENT information quantity. The file's own thesis is "attention follows
# information, not volume." Enactivism's core OPERATIONAL claim is the exact inversion: sense-making is
# NOT information-processing — an event's significance is its RELATION to the agent's CURRENT viability,
# not a property of the signal, so "the same environmental situation gets a different valence depending
# on internal state" (De Jaegher & Di Paolo, "Participatory Sense-Making", Phenom. & Cogn. Sci. 2007,
# 10.1007/s11097-007-9076-9; Di Paolo, "Autopoiesis, Adaptivity, Teleology, Agency", PCS 2005,
# 10.1007/s11097-005-9002-y — ADAPTIVITY is the capacity to regulate w.r.t. viability so encounters
# acquire valence; Colombetti, "The Feeling Body", MIT 2014 — primordial affectivity / valence as the
# lived significance of a situation; IEP "Enactivism" §"a sense-making system EVALUATES the situation as
# nutrient-rich or nutrient-poor"). The prior-preference floor is the closest sibling but is a FIXED,
# state-INDEPENDENT set — it attends [health-fail] the SAME whether the node is calm or collapsing.
#
# THE TOO-LOOSE INSTANCE this names: a threat-valenced event ([gap]/[health-fail]/[incident]) carries
# the SAME Shannon bits whether the mesh is NOMINAL or already ALERT — yet its VIABILITY significance is
# not the same: a fault arriving while the node is already degraded COMPOUNDS toward collapse and should
# attend MORE. This is the FIRST axis on the file that reads the mesh's own body-state (mesh-situation's
# committed posture, the honest-fused NOMINAL/WATCH/ALERT contract) — the enactive turn from INFORMATION
# (board-only) to SIGNIFICANCE (board × current viability). Report-only / advisory, exactly like
# --levels/--territory/--bayesian: it does NOT touch mean_bits/scored nor the --threshold wake gate.
# Honest-fusion: a missing OR STALE posture → UNKNOWN → state-neutral (×1.0), never a faked all-clear
# NOR a false alarm.
VALENCE_TAGS = set(t for t in os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_VALENCE_TAGS",
                   "incident health-fail gap stale oom deauth down fail leak error").split() if t)
_dmul = os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_STATE_MULT", "NOMINAL:1.0,WATCH:1.5,ALERT:2.0")
STATE_MULT = {}
for _kv in _dmul.split(","):
    if ":" in _kv:
        _k, _v = _kv.split(":", 1)
        try: STATE_MULT[_k.strip().upper()] = float(_v)
        except ValueError: pass
VALENCE_TTL = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_VALENCE_TTL", "1800"))  # posture older than this → UNKNOWN
SIT_STATE = os.environ.get("MESH_SITUATION_STATE", os.path.join(MESH, ".situation.state"))

def read_posture():
    """Current fused viability posture (mesh-situation's committed .situation.state contract), honestly.
    Env MESH_NOVELTY_POSTURE forces a value (test/override). A missing OR STALE state file → UNKNOWN →
    state-neutral (mult 1.0 via STATE_MULT.get default): never fake an all-clear NOR a false alarm."""
    forced = os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_POSTURE")
    if forced:
        return (forced.strip().upper(), 0)
    try:
        age = int(time.time() - os.path.getmtime(SIT_STATE))
        v = open(SIT_STATE).read().strip().upper()
    except OSError:
        return ("UNKNOWN", -1)
    if not v or age > VALENCE_TTL:
        return ("UNKNOWN", age)
    return (v, age)

def read_lines(path):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
            raw = [l.rstrip("\n") for l in f if l.strip()]
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return []
    # keep only well-formed board lines (drops the undated legacy philosophy/task dump that
    # otherwise sits at the file's physical end and pollutes the 'recent' window)
    board = [l for l in raw if BOARD.match(l)]
    return board if path == CHAT else raw

def event_type(line):
    """Coarse event signature: the bracket tag, else a generic class."""
    m = TAG.search(line)
    if m:
        return m.group(1)
    if "::" in line and "@" in line.split("::")[0]:
        return "_chat"          # an un-tagged board utterance
    return "_other"

def surprisal(p):
    return -math.log2(p) if p > 0 else 0.0

def _digamma(x):
    """ψ(x) via recurrence up to x≥6 + Abramowitz-Stegun 6.3.18 asymptotic (~1e-6 for x≥1).
    numpy-free (this tool has no numpy dep and must keep it): scipy.special.digamma is the
    reference, reimplemented here in stdlib. Anchored in --test at ψ(1)=−γ and ψ(2)=1−γ."""
    r = 0.0
    while x < 6.0:
        r -= 1.0 / x
        x += 1.0
    f = 1.0 / (x * x)
    return r + math.log(x) - 0.5 / x - f * (1/12.0 - f * (1/120.0 - f * (1/252.0)))

def bayes_bits(alpha_t, A):
    """BAYESIAN SURPRISE (Itti & Baldi) in BITS of observing ONE more event of a type whose
    current Dirichlet pseudo-count is alpha_t, total concentration A: the KL between the
    posterior Dir(α+eₜ) and the prior Dir(α). Closed form for a unit categorical update:
        KL[posterior‖prior] = ln A − ln αₜ + ψ(αₜ+1) − ψ(A+1)      (nats)
    This is how much the BELIEF MOVES, NOT how improbable the datum was (that is Shannon
    surprise −log p). The two dissociate: a KNOWN-rare type under a mature baseline has HIGH
    Shannon surprise every recurrence yet ~0 belief-move (you already know rare things happen);
    a first-seen type moves the belief maximally. KL ≥ 0 always — clamp guards digamma slop."""
    nats = math.log(A) - math.log(alpha_t) + _digamma(alpha_t + 1.0) - _digamma(A + 1.0)
    return max(0.0, nats) / math.log(2.0)

# ── GENUINE DEVIANCE vs ADAPTATION — the MATCHED-CONTROL condition (--control) ────────────────────
# LITERATURE (predictive processing & the Bayesian brain — live review 2026-08-03, angle = a concrete
# METRIC/EXPERIMENT the area uses to measure ITSELF). The field's flagship measurement of a prediction
# error is the MISMATCH NEGATIVITY: the deviant-minus-STANDARD difference wave in an oddball sequence.
# Widmann, Schröger & Wetzel, "Measuring the Genuine Mismatch Negativity in the Auditory Multi-Feature
# Paradigm", European Journal of Neuroscience 63(1):e70362, January 2026 (doi:10.1111/ejn.70362) show
# that difference is CONFOUNDED: it sums genuine deviance detection AND stimulus-specific ADAPTATION —
# the response to the repeated standard is suppressed by its own repetition, so the deviant looks big
# without any model having been violated. The remedy is not a better statistic on the same contrast, it
# is a MATCHED CONTROL CONDITION: a "cascadic" sequence in which the physically identical stimulus
# appears with the adaptational state equalised ("the trial directly preceding the control sound always
# has the same feature level (L2/F2) as the standards ... to better equalize the adaptational state")
# but violates no regularity. GENUINE MMN = deviant − CONTROL, not deviant − standard. Their verdict is
# blunt and quantitative: "Negative amplitudes in the deviant-minus-standard comparison in the auditory
# multi-feature oddball paradigm do not permit conclusions on the presence or amplitude of the genuine
# MMN." Measured at Fz: frequency −1.87 → −0.91 µV, location −1.25 → −0.49 µV (both roughly halved),
# intensity −1.91 → +0.44 µV and duration −2.29 → −0.30 µV — i.e. two of the four deviance effects
# survive the control REDUCED, and two DO NOT SURVIVE AT ALL. (Live and continuing: the adaptation-vs-
# deviance dissociation is itself still being mapped — "Complementary functional profiles of mismatch
# responses mediated by adaptation and deviance detection point to two distinct auditory short-term
# memory systems", J Neurophysiol, doi:10.1152/jn.00515.2024.)
#
# WHERE THIS FILE COMMITS THE SAME ERROR. Every axis above scores an event in its ACTUAL context against
# a baseline and reads the difference as evidence. --conditional is exactly a deviant-minus-standard
# contrast: bits(e|prev) vs the marginal bits(e), the excess read as "contextual prediction error". And
# it carries the same structural guarantee the paper warns about — p_cond is clamped `min(cand, p(cur))`
# (:476), so the conditional score can NEVER fall below the marginal and the excess is NON-NEGATIVE BY
# CONSTRUCTION. "The conditional scored higher" is therefore not a finding; it is the shape of the
# arithmetic. Worse, the excess has a purely mechanical source that mimics deviance: a Laplace-smoothed
# transition row is SPARSE, so an unlucky prev-row that simply never happened to contain `cur` yields
# cand ≪ p(cur) and several bits of "prediction error" out of finite-sample chance alone — the mesh's
# stimulus-specific adaptation. No axis on this file, and no sibling (--levels compares two REAL
# baselines, --bayesian asks how far the belief moves, --progress asks whether the sequence is getting
# compressible), ever scores the SAME event against a matched control in which the regularity is absent.
#
# THE CONTROL, transposed. Frequency-matched order surrogate: shuffle the BASELINE's order K times. The
# type multiset — hence every marginal p(t), hence the entire adaptational/rarity state — is preserved
# EXACTLY; only the sequential regularity is destroyed. Re-score the identical recent events (same
# predecessors) against each shuffled transition model. That null is the mesh's cascadic control: it is
# what the contextual excess looks like when there is nothing to violate.
#     classic  = bits(e|prev) − bits(e)              (the deviant−standard analogue: confounded)
#     genuine  = classic − mean(classic under the K order-surrogates)
#     p        = (1 + #{surrogate ≥ actual}) / (K+1)
# GENUINE = a real sequential regularity was violated · ADAPTATION = the classic excess is what the
# frequency-matched control produces anyway (the intensity-MMN case: a difference that does not survive)
# · FLAT = no classic difference to explain. Report-only / advisory, exactly like --levels/--territory/
# --bayesian/--valence: it does NOT touch mean_bits/scored nor the --threshold wake gate. Deterministic
# (fixed seed) so a number quoted from it is reproducible. The surrogate-null idiom is already mesh-wide
# (mesh-criticality, mesh-leadlag, mesh-endogeneity, mesh-correlate) — this novelty SENSE simply never
# had one, which is why its contextual excess has never been read against chance.
CONTROL_K     = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_CONTROL_K", "200"))      # surrogate baselines
CONTROL_ALPHA = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_CONTROL_ALPHA", "0.05"))
CONTROL_SEED  = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_CONTROL_SEED", "1337"))  # determinism, not secrecy
CONTROL_MIN   = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_CONTROL_MIN", "0.10")) # bits of genuine excess to call it
CONTROL_KMAX  = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_CONTROL_KMAX", "5000"))  # compute ceiling on the auto-raise

def deviance_control(btypes, pairs, K=None, alpha=None, seed=None, minbits=None, kmax=None):
    """Genuine-deviance-vs-adaptation control for the --conditional contrast (see the block above).

    btypes: the BASELINE type sequence (order matters — it is what gets surrogated).
    pairs:  [(prev_type, cur_type), ...] for the recent window (prev None at the stream head).
    Returns {type: {n, classic, null, genuine, p, cls}} — bits, per recent event type.
    """
    K = CONTROL_K if K is None else K
    alpha = CONTROL_ALPHA if alpha is None else alpha
    minbits = CONTROL_MIN if minbits is None else minbits
    if not btypes or not pairs:
        return {}
    base_c = Counter(btypes)
    V = len(base_c) + 1
    N = sum(base_c.values()) + V
    def p(t): return (base_c.get(t, 0) + 1) / N
    def build(seq):
        tr = {}
        for a, b in zip(seq, seq[1:]):
            tr.setdefault(a, Counter())[b] += 1
        return tr
    def excess(tr):
        """per-type mean CLASSIC excess bits (conditional − marginal) over the recent window."""
        acc = {}
        for prev, cur in pairs:
            row = tr.get(prev)
            if row and sum(row.values()) > 0:
                cand = min((row.get(cur, 0) + 1) / (sum(row.values()) + V), p(cur))
            else:
                cand = p(cur)                       # unseen context → marginal back-off (as analyse)
            acc.setdefault(cur, []).append(surprisal(cand) - surprisal(p(cur)))
        return {t: sum(v) / len(v) for t, v in acc.items()}
    actual = excess(build(btypes))
    # RESOLUTION. A K-surrogate permutation test cannot return a p below 1/(K+1); Bonferroni over the
    # V types tested pulls the bar to α/V. Caught on the FIRST live run (17 board types, K=200): the
    # floor 0.005 sat ABOVE α_eff=0.0029, so GENUINE was UNREACHABLE and every type read ADAPTATION —
    # a verdict manufactured by the test's own resolution, indistinguishable from a real null. Raise K
    # so significance is attainable; if a pinned-low K still cannot resolve it, say UNDERPOWERED rather
    # than report a null the instrument could not have refuted. ([[a-gate-you-have-not-seen-fail]] —
    # here the inverse: a gate that could never fire POSITIVE.)
    a_eff = alpha / max(1, len(actual))
    kmax = CONTROL_KMAX if kmax is None else kmax
    K = min(kmax, max(K, int(math.ceil(1.0 / a_eff)) - 1)) if a_eff > 0 else K
    resolvable = a_eff > 0 and (1.0 / (K + 1)) <= a_eff
    rng = random.Random(CONTROL_SEED if seed is None else seed)
    shuf = list(btypes)
    null = {t: [] for t in actual}
    for _ in range(max(1, K)):
        rng.shuffle(shuf)
        e = excess(build(shuf))
        for t in null:
            null[t].append(e.get(t, 0.0))
    out = {}
    counts = Counter(cur for _, cur in pairs)
    # One test PER TYPE → the family-wise error is ~1−(1−α)^V, not α. Measured on an i.i.d. 3-symbol
    # stream (no regularity at all, so every GENUINE is false): the uncorrected α=0.05 test minted one.
    # Bonferroni over the types actually tested (a_eff, above); conservative by construction and stated.
    for t, cls_bits in actual.items():
        ns = null[t]
        nm = sum(ns) / len(ns)
        ge = cls_bits - nm
        pv = (1 + sum(1 for x in ns if x >= cls_bits)) / (len(ns) + 1)
        cls = ("GENUINE"      if pv <= a_eff and ge >= minbits else
               "UNDERPOWERED" if not resolvable and cls_bits >= minbits else
               "ADAPTATION"   if cls_bits >= minbits else
               "FLAT")
        out[t] = dict(n=counts[t], classic=round(cls_bits, 2), null=round(nm, 2),
                      genuine=round(ge, 2), p=round(pv, 4), cls=cls, k=K, alpha_eff=round(a_eff, 5))
    return out

def _gammq(a, x):
    """Regularized UPPER incomplete gamma Q(a,x) = 1 − P(a,x) — the survival function of a
    Gamma(shape=a, scale=1). Numerical Recipes gser/gcf; pure stdlib (no numpy on this node's
    system python — see [[numpy-only-in-venvs-on-mesh-home]]). Deterministic, no RNG."""
    if x <= 0:
        return 1.0
    if a <= 0:
        return float("nan")
    if x < a + 1.0:                                   # series for P, then complement
        ap = a; s = 1.0 / a; d = s
        for _ in range(2000):
            ap += 1.0; d *= x / ap; s += d
            if abs(d) < abs(s) * 1e-15:
                break
        return max(0.0, 1.0 - s * math.exp(-x + a * math.log(x) - math.lgamma(a)))
    FPMIN = 1e-300                                    # continued fraction for Q (Lentz)
    b = x + 1.0 - a; c = 1.0 / FPMIN; d = 1.0 / b; h = d
    for i in range(1, 2000):
        an = -i * (i - a)
        b += 2.0
        d = an * d + b
        if abs(d) < FPMIN: d = FPMIN
        c = b + an / c
        if abs(c) < FPMIN: c = FPMIN
        d = 1.0 / d
        de = d * c
        h *= de
        if abs(de - 1.0) < 1e-15:
            break
    return min(1.0, math.exp(-x + a * math.log(x) - math.lgamma(a)) * h)

def _board_epoch(line):
    """Epoch seconds from a board line's leading ISO-Z stamp, or None. NEVER guesses: a
    time-only legacy stamp (`00:00:00Z`) has no date, so it returns None and the type is
    simply excluded from the timing axis rather than being anchored to a fabricated day."""
    tok = line.split(None, 1)[0] if line else ""
    try:
        return calendar.timegm(time.strptime(tok, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"))
    except (ValueError, TypeError):
        return None

def when_expectation(lines, base, recent_types, window, hi=None, miniv=None):
    """WHEN-EXPECTATION / TIME-LOCKED OMISSION PE — report-only, opt-in --when.

    LITERATURE (live review 2026-08-15: predictive processing & the Bayesian brain, angle = a
    foundational idea we MISREAD or applied too loosely). Yaron A, Shiramatsu TI, Takahashi H,
    Chao ZC, "'Nothing' Really Matters: What Omission Responses Reveal About the Predictive
    Brain", Eur J Neurosci 63(10):e70566, first published 2026-05-01, doi:10.1111/ejn.70566
    (record + abstract read first-hand via Europe PMC REST; Wiley full text is 402/paywalled
    here, so nothing below is quoted beyond the abstract). The review synthesizes the omission
    literature into TWO cooperative computational styles, and gives the empirical signatures
    that separate them, VERBATIM: "Local Regularity Encoding (LRE) generates fast, automatic
    signals through intrinsic circuit dynamics like adaptation and rebound, operating within
    constrained temporal windows. Model-Based Inference (MBI) produces slower, flexible
    predictions via distributed networks that learn specific 'what' and 'when' expectations…
    We organize these findings using empirical signatures including timing constraints,
    attention dependence, and content-specificity." Corroborating primary source, open access
    and read: Yaron, Jankowski, Badrieh, Nelken et al., "Auditory cortex neurons that encode
    negative prediction errors respond to omissions of sounds in a predictable sequence", PLoS
    Biology 2025, doi:10.1371/journal.pbio.3003242 — omission responses there are BOTH
    content-specific ("59 (66%) were selective for OP omissions") AND explicitly time-locked,
    measured in "a 5–120 ms post-omission window" aligned to "the expected onset of the omitted
    tone (time = 0 ms)".

    WHAT WE APPLIED TOO LOOSELY. This file already carries an omission axis (2026-07-29, see the
    block inside analyse()) and its header cites Furutachi & Hofer's positive-vs-negative PE
    dissociation. Against the review's own two signatures it is HALF the mechanism:
      • content-specificity — EMBODIED. The axis is per-type; each tag's silence is scored on
        that tag's own rate. It is not a generic "the board went quiet" gap detector.
      • the "WHEN" expectation — ABSENT. `obits = −window·log2(1−q)` scores silence against a
        RATE across a fixed COUNT window. A count window is a temporal constraint imposed by the
        INSTRUMENT; it is not an interval LEARNED from the producer. By the review's taxonomy
        that is the LRE half ("constrained temporal windows"), not the MBI half that learns
        "when". The mesh named the axis after the model-based mechanism and shipped the local one.
    The statistical form of the same error: (1−q)^N is a memoryless Bernoulli/Poisson arrival
    model. It is exactly right at CV=1 and wrong in BOTH directions off it — for a REGULAR
    producer (a cron reflex; CV→0) it badly UNDER-states how overdue a silence is, and for a
    BURSTY one (a mind posting a cluster then going quiet; CV≫1) it OVER-states it. The board's
    timestamps have carried the missing dimension the whole time (analyse() already parses one
    at the first-seen-device split); no axis in this file has ever read them as an interval.

    THE INSTRUMENT. Per type, from the board's own ISO-Z stamps:
      intervals → mean μ, sd σ, CV = σ/μ → REGULARITY class (the review's "timing constraint"
      signature): REGULAR (CV < WHEN_REG_CV) · POISSON (…< WHEN_BURST_CV) · BURSTY (≥).
      Δt = seconds since the type's LAST arrival, measured against the tape's last stamp (NOT
      wallclock) so the verdict is a pure function of the tape — deterministic, replayable, and
      identical in --test and in production. Two independent survival estimates of P(silence at
      least this long):
        wbits (parametric) = −log2 Q(k, Δt/θ), a Gamma renewal law fitted by moments,
              k = 1/CV², θ = μ/k. This NESTS the current model: at CV=1, k=1, Q = e^(−Δt/μ) —
              the memoryless case — so every bit of difference from the count axis is the
              regularity correction and nothing else.
        ebits (distribution-free) = −log2[(#{iv > Δt} + 1)/(n_iv + 1)], the empirical survival
              with the +1 that makes it a bound rather than a zero.
      VERDICT USES THE CONSERVATIVE ONE, min(wbits, ebits), and both are always printed.

    WHY THE SECOND LEG IS LOAD-BEARING, not decoration. A Gamma fitted to 9 intervals of a
    highly regular producer has an astronomically thin tail: on this node's live board
    [board-shrink-averted] (CV 0.20, 9 intervals) reads 996 BITS overdue under the fitted law.
    That number is manufactured by extrapolating a 9-sample fit far past its own support. The
    empirical leg cannot exceed log2(n_iv + 1) — 3.32 bits from 9 intervals — so it refuses on
    exactly the types where the parametric leg is most confident. Same shape as the resolution
    floor already earned by --control (a K-surrogate test cannot report p < 1/(K+1)) and by
    --recover's identifiability work in mesh-precision: an instrument must state the resolution
    it actually has. A type whose ceiling sits under the bar reads UNDERPOWERED — never a null
    verdict the sample could not have refuted, and never a positive one it could not have earned.

    HONEST BOUNDARIES (the point, not omissions). (a) A board POST is not the producer's run —
    a reflex that runs every 600s and posts only when a condition trips has a board interval
    law that is the CONDITION's, not the cadence's; this axis measures the board, and says so.
    (b) ~/.mesh/chat.log is a sliding window, so a type's FIRST interval is unobserved
    (left-censoring) and every n_iv is today's answer — re-derive, never quote. (c) The Gamma is
    a renewal fit: it assumes successive intervals are independent, which a clustered producer
    violates in a way CV records but does not repair. (d) Lines whose stamp is not a full ISO-Z
    date are dropped, not dated. Report-only: it does NOT touch mean_bits/scored, the omission
    axis, or the --threshold wake gate — rewiring SPEND stays the steward's.
    """
    hi = LEVELS_HI if hi is None else hi
    miniv = WHEN_MINIV if miniv is None else miniv
    arrivals = defaultdict(list)
    for l in lines:
        e = _board_epoch(l)
        if e is not None:
            arrivals[event_type(l)].append(e)
    if not arrivals:
        return {}
    now = max(v[-1] for v in arrivals.values())
    q_total = sum(base.values()) or 1
    out = {}
    for t, times in arrivals.items():
        times = sorted(times)
        iv = [b - a for a, b in zip(times, times[1:]) if b > a]
        n = len(iv)
        ceiling = math.log2(n + 1) if n else 0.0
        # what the COUNT axis (the shipped omission term) says about this same type, so the two
        # verdicts are compared on one line instead of by eye across two reports.
        c = base.get(t, 0)
        q = c / q_total
        cnt_gated = (t in recent_types) or (q * window) < OMIT_MINEXP or q >= 1.0
        obits = -window * math.log2(1.0 - q) if 0.0 < q < 1.0 else 0.0
        cnt_calls = (not cnt_gated) and obits >= hi
        if n < miniv or n < 2:          # `or n < 2` is a HARD floor, not the tunable one: a CV needs
                                        # two intervals to exist at all, so miniv=0 (the RED-first knob
                                        # in --test) must not reach the variance below.
            out[t] = dict(n_iv=n, cls="UNSCORABLE", reg="UNSCORABLE", cv=None, mu=None, dt=None,
                          wbits=None, ebits=None, cons=None, ceiling=round(ceiling, 2),
                          obits=round(obits, 2), cnt_calls=cnt_calls, agree=None)
            continue
        mu = sum(iv) / n
        var = sum((x - mu) ** 2 for x in iv) / (n - 1) if n > 1 else 0.0
        cv = (math.sqrt(var) / mu) if mu > 0 else 0.0
        k = min(1.0 / (max(cv, WHEN_CVFLOOR) ** 2), WHEN_KMAX)
        theta = mu / k if k > 0 else mu
        dt = now - times[-1]
        s_par = min(max(_gammq(k, dt / theta) if theta > 0 else 1.0, 1e-300), 1.0)
        wbits = -math.log2(s_par)
        s_emp = (sum(1 for x in iv if x > dt) + 1) / (n + 1)
        ebits = -math.log2(s_emp)
        cons = min(wbits, ebits)
        reg = ("REGULAR" if cv < WHEN_REG_CV else
               "POISSON" if cv < WHEN_BURST_CV else "BURSTY")
        when_calls = cons >= hi
        if ceiling < hi:
            # the sample cannot reach the bar at all — refuse in the direction the parametric
            # leg was about to over-claim, and stay silent where it was not claiming anything.
            cls = "UNDERPOWERED" if wbits >= hi else "QUIET"
            agree = None
        else:
            cls = "SILENT" if when_calls else "QUIET"
            agree = ("UNDER-CALLED" if when_calls and not cnt_calls else
                     "OVER-CALLED"  if cnt_calls and not when_calls else "AGREE")
        out[t] = dict(n_iv=n, cls=cls, reg=reg, cv=round(cv, 2), mu=round(mu, 1), dt=round(dt, 1),
                      wbits=round(wbits, 2), ebits=round(ebits, 2), cons=round(cons, 2),
                      ceiling=round(ceiling, 2), obits=round(obits, 2),
                      cnt_calls=cnt_calls, agree=agree)
    return out

# ── UNCERTAINTY-DRIVEN vs ERROR-DRIVEN BOUNDARIES — two control signals, not one ───────────────────
# LIVE LITERATURE (predictive processing & the Bayesian brain, read 2026-08-20):
#   Nguyen TT, Etzel JA, Bezdek MA, Zacks JM — "Multiple event segmentation mechanisms in the human
#   brain", eLife 107955 (reviewed preprint v3, 2026-07-07), doi:10.7554/eLife.107955.3
#   (elifesciences.org/articles/107955; v2 record elifesciences.org/reviewed-preprints/107955).
#   Event Segmentation Theory has always said a model is torn down and rebuilt when PREDICTION ERROR
#   spikes. This paper separates that from a second, computationally distinct control signal —
#   PREDICTION UNCERTAINTY — and finds BOTH, dissociated in the brain and in behaviour, VERBATIM:
#     "Both error-driven and uncertainty-driven boundaries were associated with unique pattern shifts."
#     "Error-driven boundaries were associated with early pattern shifts in ventrolateral prefrontal
#      areas, followed by pattern stabilization in prefrontal and temporal areas. Uncertainty-driven
#      boundaries were linked to shifts in parietal regions within the dorsal attention network, with
#      minimal subsequent stabilization."
#     "Even though error-driven and uncertainty-driven event model updating were associated with the
#      same brain regions, the two updating mechanisms were associated with distinct temporal dynamics."
#   And the property that makes uncertainty a different KIND of signal, not a weaker error signal:
#     "The advantage of relying on prediction uncertainty to detect event boundaries is that it is
#      inherently PROACTIVE: the cognitive system can start looking for cues about what might come
#      next BEFORE the next event starts."
#   Their earlier modelling arm (Nguyen et al. 2024, cited there): "both error-driven and
#   uncertainty-driven updating signals aligned with human segmentation and categorization judgments,
#   but that uncertainty-driven segmentation aligned significantly better."
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DID — every axis here is ERROR-DRIVEN, without exception.
#   marginal −log P(e) · --conditional −log P(e|prev) · --bayesian (KL the event MOVED the belief) ·
#   --levels (deviance at two timescales) · --territory · --when (how OVERDUE an arrival is) ·
#   --features (which LEVEL was violated) · --control (is the excess genuine) · --progress (is the
#   error FALLING). Every one of them is a function of an event that ALREADY ARRIVED: they score the
#   RESIDUAL. Nothing in this file scores the SPREAD of the model's own next-step distribution, which
#   is a property of the CONTEXT and is computable BEFORE the next line is posted. (Checked first: the
#   genome's one neighbour is mesh-reflex-health's AMBIGUITY axis — EFE ambiguity IS "the expected
#   conditional entropy of observations given states" — but it prices how often an ORGAN answers n/a
#   and holds no sequential model, so it cannot speak about a successor at all.) So the wake gate this file feeds is structurally REACTIVE: the mesh can only ever
#   notice that it has already been surprised, never that it has stopped being able to predict.
#   The two are not the same event. A context whose successor distribution has gone flat emits NO
#   surprising line — every successor is ordinary, each one individually cheap — while the model
#   holding that context has quietly stopped being a model. That is an event boundary the error axis
#   cannot represent at any threshold.
#
# THE INSTRUMENT. One first-order model, both signals read off the SAME row so the comparison is not
# confounded by two models:
#   ERROR  bits = −log2 P(x_t | ctx), floored at the marginal exactly as p_cond() does — this IS the
#          number --conditional reports, recomputed here so the pair is commensurable.
#   UNCERT cons = the conditional entropy H(P(· | ctx)) of that same row, in bits, and it uses NO
#          part of x_t. Reported as a REDUCTION against the marginal entropy H_marg: a context is
#          UNPREDICTIVE when its own entropy buys nothing over knowing nothing at all.
# TWO LEGS AND THE CONSERVATIVE MIN, the same discipline --when and --control earned:
#   h_smooth = entropy of the Laplace-smoothed row over the whole alphabet — what a consumer of this
#              model would actually use, and BIASED UP: an unseen or thin context is maximally
#              "uncertain" BY CONSTRUCTION, not by evidence (prior_share = V/(n+V) states how much of
#              the row is prior rather than board).
#   h_mm     = the plug-in entropy of the RAW row + the Miller–Madow correction (k_obs−1)/(2n ln2),
#              which repairs the plug-in estimator's opposite, DOWNWARD bias at small n.
#   cons = min(h_smooth, h_mm) — conservative against the claim this mode exists to make.
# AND THE RESOLUTION IT ACTUALLY HAS: n draws cannot exhibit empirical entropy above log2(min(n, V)).
#   A context under that ceiling reads UNDERPOWERED — never "predictable", never "unpredictable".
#   A context never seen as a predecessor (n = 0) reads NO-MODEL: its smoothed entropy is the alphabet
#   maximum and means only that nothing was ever learned here. Calling that "uncertain" would be the
#   unprepared-channel fallacy — the response magnitude reporting the instrument's own blankness.
# PROACTIVE, demonstrated not asserted: `next` is computed from the LAST line's type alone, with no
#   successor in hand at all. It is the only verdict in this file about an event that does not exist
#   yet, and dropping every future line cannot change it.
# REPORT-ONLY: mean_bits, --threshold, --edge and every other mode are untouched.
UNC_MINSUP  = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_UNC_MINSUP", "8"))    # min observed transitions before a row may be judged
UNC_FRAC    = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_UNC_FRAC", "0.9"))  # frac of the MARGINAL entropy above which a context is UNPREDICTIVE
UNC_MINBASE = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_UNC_MINBASE", "60"))  # min baseline lines before anything may be said

def _h_bits(ps):
    return -sum(q * math.log2(q) for q in ps if q > 0)

def uncertainty_boundaries(lines, window=40, hi=None, minsup=None, frac=None, minbase=None):
    """PREDICTION UNCERTAINTY as a second, PROACTIVE boundary signal — report-only, opt-in.

    See the header block above for the source (Nguyen/Etzel/Bezdek/Zacks, eLife 2026) and the
    instrument. Returns None (honest n/a) when the board cannot support a transition model.
    """
    hi      = LEVELS_HI    if hi      is None else hi
    minsup  = UNC_MINSUP   if minsup  is None else minsup
    frac    = UNC_FRAC     if frac    is None else frac
    minbase = UNC_MINBASE  if minbase is None else minbase
    types = [event_type(l) for l in lines]
    if window < 1 or len(types) <= window or len(types) - window < minbase:
        return None
    baseline, recent = types[:-window], types[-window:]
    base = Counter(baseline)
    V = len(base) + 1                       # alphabet incl. the unseen-type slot (as p() does)
    N = sum(base.values()) + V
    h_marg = _h_bits([(base[t] + 1) / N for t in base] + [1.0 / N])
    bar_u = frac * h_marg
    trans = {}
    for a, b in zip(baseline, baseline[1:]):
        trans.setdefault(a, Counter())[b] += 1

    def row(ctx):
        r = trans.get(ctx) or Counter()
        n = sum(r.values())
        k_obs = len(r)
        d = n + V
        h_smooth = _h_bits([(r.get(t, 0) + 1) / d for t in base] + [1.0 / d])
        prior_share = V / d
        if n <= 0:                          # never seen as a predecessor: nothing was learned here
            return dict(n=0, k_obs=0, h_smooth=h_smooth, h_emp=None, h_mm=None, cons=None,
                        ceiling=0.0, prior_share=prior_share, cls="NO-MODEL", _r=r, _d=d)
        h_emp = _h_bits([c / n for c in r.values()])
        h_mm = min(h_emp + (k_obs - 1) / (2.0 * n * math.log(2)), math.log2(V))
        ceiling = math.log2(min(n, V))
        cons = min(h_smooth, h_mm)
        cls = "UNDERPOWERED" if (n < minsup or ceiling < bar_u) else None
        return dict(n=n, k_obs=k_obs, h_smooth=h_smooth, h_emp=h_emp, h_mm=h_mm, cons=cons,
                    ceiling=ceiling, prior_share=prior_share, cls=cls, _r=r, _d=d)

    def err_bits(st, obs):
        """−log2 P(obs|ctx) with p_cond()'s exact semantics: marginal back-off + marginal floor."""
        p_marg = (base.get(obs, 0) + 1) / N
        if st["n"] <= 0:
            return surprisal(p_marg)
        return surprisal(min((st["_r"].get(obs, 0) + 1) / st["_d"], p_marg))

    rows, es, us = [], [], []
    start = len(types) - window
    for i, obs in enumerate(recent):
        ctx = types[start + i - 1] if start + i - 1 >= 0 else None
        st = row(ctx)
        bits = err_bits(st, obs)
        e_hi = bits >= hi
        if st["cls"]:                       # NO-MODEL / UNDERPOWERED — refuse the uncertainty verdict
            cls, u_hi = st["cls"], None
        else:
            u_hi = st["cons"] >= bar_u
            cls = ("BOTH" if (e_hi and u_hi) else "UNCERTAINTY-DRIVEN" if u_hi
                   else "ERROR-DRIVEN" if e_hi else "-")
            es.append(bits); us.append(st["cons"])
        rows.append(dict(i=i, ctx=ctx, obs=obs, bits=round(bits, 2), e_hi=e_hi, u_hi=u_hi, cls=cls,
                         n=st["n"], k_obs=st["k_obs"],
                         cons=None if st["cons"] is None else round(st["cons"], 2),
                         h_smooth=round(st["h_smooth"], 2),
                         h_mm=None if st["h_mm"] is None else round(st["h_mm"], 2),
                         gain=None if st["cons"] is None else round(h_marg - st["cons"], 2),
                         ceiling=round(st["ceiling"], 2), prior_share=round(st["prior_share"], 3)))
    # THE PROACTIVE READ: the next line has not been posted. No successor is used anywhere below.
    nctx = types[-1]
    ns = row(nctx)
    nxt = dict(ctx=nctx, n=ns["n"], k_obs=ns["k_obs"], ceiling=round(ns["ceiling"], 2),
               cons=None if ns["cons"] is None else round(ns["cons"], 2),
               prior_share=round(ns["prior_share"], 3),
               k_eff=None if ns["cons"] is None else round(2 ** ns["cons"], 1),
               cls=ns["cls"] or ("UNPREDICTIVE" if ns["cons"] >= bar_u else "PREDICTIVE"),
               top=[t for t, _ in ns["_r"].most_common(3)])
    return dict(window=window, baseline=len(baseline), alphabet=V, h_marg=round(h_marg, 3),
                bar_u=round(bar_u, 3), bar_e=hi, minsup=minsup, frac=frac,
                counts=dict(Counter(r["cls"] for r in rows)), rows=rows, next=nxt,
                r_eu=_feat_pearson(es, us), n_scored=len(es))

# ── FEATURE-SPECIFIC PREDICTION ERROR — surprise has a LEVEL, and one scalar cannot carry two ──────
# LIVE LITERATURE (predictive processing / Bayesian brain, read 2026-08-18):
#   Richter D, Uran C, Vinck M, de Lange FP — "Feature-specific predictive processing: What's in a
#   prediction error?", Imaging Neuroscience (MIT Press), 2025-12-18, doi:10.1162/IMAG.a.1061
#   (open: PMC12715616). The one sentence: **"a stimulus may be both predicted and surprising,
#   depending on the specific features."** Their evidence that the LEVEL of the violated feature is
#   an axis of its own, not a magnitude: Richter et al. 2024 (fMRI) — every visual area *including
#   V1* was upregulated by HIGH-level (object-identity) surprise and NOT by low-level (orientation/
#   contrast) surprise, inverting the area's own tuning; Richter et al. 2025 (EEG) — that high-level
#   modulation lands <200 ms; Heilbron & de Lange 2025 (mouse) — same in mouse V1, strongest in
#   superficial layers; Uran et al. 2022 (macaque) — in ONE area the two levels ride DIFFERENT
#   observables: V1 firing rate tracks high-level predictability, narrow-band gamma (30–80 Hz)
#   tracks low-level. Their idiom for why the high level is the behaviourally relevant one and the
#   easier to predict: **"rain vs individual drops of rain."**
#   Companion live source (the same month, the dissent): Westerberg JA et al., "Hierarchical
#   interactions between sensory cortices defy predictive coding", Trends Cogn Sci 2026;30(2):110-123,
#   doi:10.1016/j.tics.2025.09.018 — feedback ENHANCES the predicted representation rather than
#   suppressing it. Both papers land on the same operational point from opposite directions: the
#   observable "response magnitude" does not name which feature was violated.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DID. Every mode above — marginal, --conditional, --bayesian, --levels, --territory,
# --progress, --tempering, --when, --control — scores events drawn from ONE alphabet, `event_type()`:
# the bracket marker. That is a single, and specifically a LOW, feature: the surface form of the
# token. So the tool cannot represent an event that is unremarkable in form and violating in role
# (nor the reverse), and the wake gate it feeds picks by the low axis alone.
#
# MEASURED ON THIS NODE'S BOARD (~/.mesh/chat.log, 3000 lines, 2026-08-18 — every figure is today's
# answer; chat.log is a sliding window). Three levels, each with its OWN baseline:
#   form  = the literal marker as typed (alphabet 101, H 4.62b)   ← what event_type() sees
#   actor = the emitting window/organ  (alphabet  87, H 5.19b)
#   role  = the board grammar mesh-promises already parses (task|taking|done|verify|fyi + `sense`
#           for every organ marker outside it) — the COARSE level, the one that is easier to predict
#   pairwise r over the last 600 events:  r(form,role) = **−0.41** · r(actor,role) = +0.02
#   top-decile agreement between a `form` gate (today's scalar) and a `role` gate: **1 of 60**
#   role-top events sitting BELOW the median form-surprise (invisible to today's scalar): **33/60**,
#     and they are `done/genome`, `done/land`, `task/discover`, `taking/genome` — the claim grammar
#   form-top events sitting AT the role axis FLOOR (surface-only — the raindrops): **59/60**,
#     and they are `[criticality-signal-lost]`, `[note3-light-raw]`, `[health-ok]`, `[bt-exposure]`
# The two axes are not merely non-redundant here, they are ANTI-correlated, and structurally so: the
# board holds two populations — frequent coordination words (low form-surprise, high role-surprise)
# and rare one-off organ markers (the reverse). Today's scalar wakes on drops of rain.
#
# NORMALIZATION, stated plainly because it is what makes the levels comparable and is otherwise a
# trick: for a marker inside the grammar, form and role are the SAME event, so the RAW bits are
# near-identical (live: `done` = 3.03b as a form, 2.98b as a role — they differ only by each level's
# smoothing denominator). Each level's surprisal is divided by THAT level's own baseline entropy,
# giving "how
# surprising is this event for this feature" — self-calibrating against the live corpus, never an
# assumed 0..1 (doctrine: calibrate a derived axis against the REAL corpus). A dominance verdict is
# therefore a statement about levels, not a second opinion about bits.
# REPORT-ONLY: this adds no gate. mean_bits, --threshold and --edge are untouched.
FEAT_LEVELS = ("form", "actor", "role")
# the board grammar mesh-promises' LINE regex parses; anything else is an organ report
FEAT_GRAMMAR = ("task", "taking", "done", "verify", "fyi", "sense")
FEAT_LINE = re.compile(r'^\d{2,4}[-:0-9T]*Z?\s+(\S+)\s+::\s*(.*)$')
FEAT_MARK = re.compile(r'\[([^\]]{1,40})\]')
FEAT_MIN = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_FEAT_MIN", "60"))   # min baseline lines to say anything

def feat_events(lines):
    """Decompose each board line into its feature vector (form, actor, role)."""
    out = []
    for l in lines:
        m = FEAT_LINE.match(l)
        if not m:
            continue
        who, body = m.group(1), m.group(2)
        t = FEAT_MARK.search(body)
        form = t.group(1) if t else "_untagged"
        role = form.lower() if form.lower() in FEAT_GRAMMAR else "sense"
        out.append(dict(form=form, actor=who.split("@")[0], role=role))
    return out

def _feat_pearson(a, b):
    n = len(a)
    if n < 2:
        return None
    ma, mb = sum(a) / n, sum(b) / n
    num = sum((x - ma) * (y - mb) for x, y in zip(a, b))
    den = math.sqrt(sum((x - ma) ** 2 for x in a) * sum((y - mb) ** 2 for y in b))
    return (num / den) if den > 0 else None

def features(lines, window=40, tail=600):
    """Per-level (form/actor/role) normalized surprisal + the levels' disagreement.

    Returns None when the baseline cannot support the claim (honest n/a, never a fabricated calm)."""
    ev = feat_events(lines)
    if len(ev) < FEAT_MIN + window:
        return None
    base, recent = ev[:-window], ev[-window:]
    st = {}
    for lv in FEAT_LEVELS:
        c = Counter(e[lv] for e in base)
        N = sum(c.values())
        K = len(c) + 1                       # add-1 smoothing reserves mass for the unseen type
        H = sum((v / N) * -math.log2((v + 1) / (N + K)) for v in c.values())
        st[lv] = dict(c=c, N=N, K=K, H=H, types=len(c))

    def nb(lv, key):
        s = st[lv]
        bits = -math.log2((s["c"].get(key, 0) + 1) / (s["N"] + s["K"]))
        return bits / s["H"] if s["H"] > 0 else 0.0

    rows = []
    for e in recent:
        v = {lv: nb(lv, e[lv]) for lv in FEAT_LEVELS}
        dom = max(v, key=v.get)
        rows.append(dict(form=e["form"], actor=e["actor"], role=e["role"],
                         n={k: round(x, 3) for k, x in v.items()},
                         dom=dom, spread=round(max(v.values()) - min(v.values()), 3)))

    # do the levels agree? — over a longer tail than the window, so the answer is not one window's luck
    tl = ev[-min(tail, len(ev)):]
    vecs = {lv: [nb(lv, e[lv]) for e in tl] for lv in FEAT_LEVELS}
    corr = {}
    for i, a in enumerate(FEAT_LEVELS):
        for b in FEAT_LEVELS[i + 1:]:
            corr[f"{a}~{b}"] = _feat_pearson(vecs[a], vecs[b])

    # what a LOW-level gate picks vs what the HIGH-level one picks (this file's own wake gate is low)
    K = max(1, len(tl) // 10)
    order = lambda lv: sorted(range(len(tl)), key=lambda i: -vecs[lv][i])[:K]
    topf, topr = order("form"), order("role")
    fl_role = min(vecs["role"])                      # the role axis' floor — ties make a median useless
    gate = dict(k=K, n=len(tl), overlap=len(set(topf) & set(topr)),
                form_top_at_role_floor=sum(1 for i in topf if vecs["role"][i] <= fl_role + 1e-9),
                role_top_below_median_form=sum(
                    1 for i in topr
                    if vecs["form"][i] < sorted(vecs["form"])[len(tl) // 2]),
                form_top=Counter(tl[i]["form"] for i in topf).most_common(5),
                role_top=Counter(tl[i]["role"] + "/" + tl[i]["actor"] for i in topr).most_common(5))
    return dict(levels={lv: dict(types=st[lv]["types"], h_bits=round(st[lv]["H"], 3))
                        for lv in FEAT_LEVELS},
                rows=rows, corr={k: (round(v, 3) if v is not None else None) for k, v in corr.items()},
                gate=gate, window=window, baseline=len(base))

def analyse(window=40, conditional=False, control=False, when=False):
    lines = read_lines(CHAT)
    if len(lines) < 10:
        return None
    recent = lines[-window:]
    # ── EIGENFORM / DEGENERATE-FIXED-POINT BLIND SPOT (von Foerster; Kauffman) ───────────────────
    # 2nd-order cybernetics cross-domain transfer (LITERATURE 2026-06-21): von Foerster — "objects
    # are tokens for EIGENBEHAVIORS"; an object/state is the stable FIXED POINT of the observer's own
    # recursive operation, T(Object)=Object (Kauffman, "Eigenforms — Objects as Tokens for
    # Eigenbehaviors", Cybernetics & Human Knowing, 2003-05; von Foerster, "Objects: Tokens for
    # (Eigen-)Behaviors", 1976). The deep point: the observer is PART of the observed, so a
    # self-referential signal can converge to a fixed point that has DECOUPLED from the world.
    #
    # THIS function is reflexive in exactly that sense: the baseline IS the system's OWN past output
    # (lines[:-window] of the same board mesh-novelty also writes to via --edge/--stream). That makes
    # the novelty score an eigenform of a self-observing loop — and it has the UNDER-COVERED failure
    # mode (the COUPLED-but-decoupling direction, sibling to the honest-fusion DECOUPLED guards):
    #   • A PERSISTENT anomaly is ABSORBED into "normal." Once a pathological event type recurs across
    #     enough lines it accretes into `base` (below) → its p(t) rises → its surprisal -log P FALLS →
    #     it stops being novel. The baseline becomes its own confirmation: a DEGENERATE fixed point
    #     (reproduces regardless of whether the thing is actually a problem). Boiling-frog / self-
    #     confirmation. Neither marginal surprisal NOR --edge catches it: a gradual accretion slips
    #     under the ±0.5b shift floor, and absorption LOWERS mean novelty (--edge watches for a rise).
    # VERIFIED THIS SESSION: the home_state↔desk re-flood — the SAME spurious CORRELATION/CONNECTION
    # dispatch + [done] hit the board 4× (10:12/10:15/10:29/11:02). After the first 1-2, those types
    # are in the baseline → the 3rd/4th score LOW novelty. A human caught the pathological RECURRENCE
    # by reasoning; this reflex structurally CANNOT — its baseline self-confirmed. (The seed-laundering
    # fix in mesh-correlate stopped the SOURCE; this names why the novelty SENSE was blind to it.)
    #
    # HELD FIX (instrument-first, steward/operator lands — behavioral): add a SECOND axis beside
    # surprisal-vs-baseline — a BASELINE-DRIFT / eigenform-stability check: flag an event type whose
    # frequency is RISING across successive baselines (an anomaly accreting into normal) even as its
    # marginal surprise falls. I.e. test whether the baseline is itself a STABLE fixed point or is
    # absorbing — a persistent-anomaly detector is the exact complement to a rare-event detector.
    # WHY HELD: a real regime change (the mesh genuinely growing a new normal) looks identical to a
    # pathological accretion at the signal level — separating them needs a reference the loop does NOT
    # author (a fixed long-baseline, or operator/queue-tend confirmation), else it just flags all
    # growth. Validate against the board history before gating a SPEND signal (this gates mind wake).
    # See [[fusion-tools-distinguish-empty-from-failed]] (DECOUPLED dir), [[delta-channels-need-gate]],
    # [[review-coupling-constitution-fallacy-mesh-card-2026-06-21]] (the membership-direction sibling).
    #
    # ── VOLATILITY-BLIND THRESHOLD: the wake bar is FIXED; it should track environmental change-rate ──
    # LITERATURE (live review, what's NEW in predictive processing 2023-2026): the Bayesian-brain
    # frontier most used right now is the HIERARCHICAL GAUSSIAN FILTER (Mathys et al., "A Bayesian
    # foundation for individual learning under uncertainty", Front. Hum. Neurosci. 2011; "Uncertainty in
    # perception and the HGF", 2014) — still the 2023-2026 workhorse of computational psychiatry, where
    # aberrant VOLATILITY estimation indexes psychosis/hallucination (precision-weighted prediction-error
    # studies, biorxiv 2025.07.07.662254; Frontiers Psychiatry 2025, fpsyt.2025.1713833). The HGF's key
    # move beyond flat precision-weighting: a HIGHER level that tracks how fast the hidden cause is
    # CHANGING (volatility), and the learning-rate / surprise-bar is scaled by it — in a VOLATILE regime a
    # big delta is EXPECTED (low surprise, learn slowly), in a STABLE regime the same delta is alarming
    # (high surprise, learn fast). Precision = inverse variance of the signal NOW; volatility = variance of
    # the GENERATIVE rate-of-change over time. Two different levels of the same hierarchy.
    #
    # THE GAP THIS NAMES: this reflex's wake threshold is a CONSTANT — `--threshold B bits`, a fixed CLI
    # arg (usage :25) compared against `score` with NO awareness of the current regime. So the same B both
    # floods minds during a legitimately churny window (operator arriving + devices appearing + arrivals
    # firing = lots of real surprisal that is EXPECTED given the volatility) AND can stay silent in a
    # dead-quiet period where a single odd event is the only thing that matters. The mesh already FELT this
    # as the novelty score-wobble flood ([[delta-channels-need-gate]]) — patched downstream with a static
    # --gate, never with a volatility-scaled bar. mesh-precision supplies a sense's precision (noise NOW);
    # NOTHING estimates volatility (change-rate OVER TIME) to set the threshold.
    #
    # DISTINCT from the three siblings on this file: (a) mesh-precision weights AMONG senses by signal noise
    # — orthogonal level (precision, not volatility); (b) the eigenform block ABOVE is the baseline ABSORBING
    # a persistent anomaly (a decoupling fixed point) — a first-order-MEAN pathology, whereas this is the
    # SECOND-ORDER VARIANCE setting an ADAPTIVE bar; (c) the reducible/irreducible-surprise block BELOW
    # (:136, Schmidhuber) is WHICH surprise is worth chasing — this is HOW MUCH surprise should wake, given
    # the regime. They compose: volatility scales the bar, aleatoric-discount picks the type, eigenform-drift
    # guards the baseline.
    # HELD FIX (instrument-first, steward/operator lands — behavioral, gates mind WAKE so validate first):
    # estimate recent volatility (rolling variance/EWMA of the surprisal series, or event-distribution
    # switch-rate over a short window) and SCALE the effective wake threshold by it — raise B in a volatile
    # window, lower it in a quiet one — so attention follows surprise-relative-to-regime, not raw bits. WHY
    # HELD: a volatility spike and a genuine regime change are degenerate at the signal level (same caveat as
    # the eigenform fix); a wrongly-low bar in a quiet window could chatter minds — needs a reference the
    # loop does not author. The mechanism is named here; the behavioral wiring is the steward's.
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    baseline = lines[:-window] if len(lines) > window else lines
    # baseline distribution over event types (add-1 / Laplace smoothing)
    base = Counter(event_type(l) for l in baseline)
    V = len(base) + 1                       # +1 for the unseen-type mass
    N = sum(base.values()) + V
    def p(t): return (base.get(t, 0) + 1) / N
    # CONDITIONAL (predictive-coding) mode: a first-order Markov forward model P(eᵢ|eᵢ₋₁) learnt
    # from the baseline transitions; surprise = -log P(eᵢ|eᵢ₋₁), the residual against the context
    # prediction. A context never seen as a predecessor backs off to the marginal p(t) (so it never
    # scores LESS surprising than marginal would). This "explains away" predictable sequences
    # (taking→done) while a contextually-unexpected transition stays high-bit.
    # ── NOISY-TV / REDUCIBLE vs IRREDUCIBLE SURPRISE (Schmidhuber; aleatoric≠epistemic) ──────────────
    # LITERATURE — information theory of agency (predictive information), the KNOWN FAILURE MODE
    # (2026-06-21): the NOISY-TV PROBLEM (Schmidhuber 1991, "A possibility for implementing curiosity
    # and boredom in model-building neural controllers"; named + measured by Burda, Edwards, Pathak et
    # al., "Large-Scale Study of Curiosity-Driven Learning", ICML 2019; Mavor-Parker et al., "How to
    # Stay Curious while Avoiding Noisy TVs using Aleatoric Uncertainty Estimation", ICML 2022; still
    # open per "Beyond Noisy-TVs: Noise-Robust Exploration via Learning Progress Monitoring",
    # arXiv:2509.25438, 2025). An agent that rewards RAW prediction error / information-gain fixates on
    # a STOCHASTIC source — TV static — that is endlessly "surprising" but UNLEARNABLE: the surprise is
    # IRREDUCIBLE (aleatoric) noise, not REDUCIBLE (epistemic) novelty, so observing it teaches nothing
    # yet pays maximal intrinsic reward forever. The principled fix is to value LEARNING PROGRESS —
    # the REDUCTION of prediction error over time (compression progress) — not the instantaneous error.
    # WHERE THIS REFLEX COMMITS THE GAP: BOTH scores here are instantaneous error. Marginal surprisal
    # -log P(e) and the --conditional residual -log P(e|prev) each score a source by how surprising it
    # is RIGHT NOW; NEITHER asks whether that surprise is FALLING as the baseline accumulates (learnable)
    # or PINNED high because the source is intrinsically random (a noisy-TV). Crucially --conditional does
    # NOT fix this: it explains away PREDICTABLE STRUCTURE (taking->done), but an aleatoric source HAS no
    # structure to explain away, so its conditional error stays maximal — by construction the predictive-
    # coding upgrade cannot reduce irreducible noise. So a genuinely random board source (a flapping
    # sensor's jittering event type, a metric that wobbles every window — the "novelty score-wobble
    # flood", [[delta-channels-need-gate]]) reads HIGH novelty EVERY window → use-case-2 ("wake on HIGH
    # novelty") wakes expensive minds on noise forever, and the digest top-5 (use-case-1) surfaces static.
    # That is the noisy-TV: this novelty SENSE is the curiosity reward, and it has no learnability filter.
    # HELD FIX (instrument-first, steward/operator lands — behavioral): a LEARNING-PROGRESS axis — track
    # an event type's surprisal across SUCCESSIVE windows; value a type whose surprise is DECLINING as it
    # accretes (epistemic — the model is learning it) and DISCOUNT a type whose surprise stays PINNED
    # high despite repeated exposure (aleatoric — a noisy-TV) before it can gate a SPEND/wake signal.
    # WHY HELD: estimating learnability needs a multi-window history this single-pass call does not keep,
    # and it must not discount a source that is high-surprise because it is genuinely NEW each window
    # (real ongoing novelty) vs random — separable only with a reducibility estimate validated against
    # board history. Gate nothing until validated (this is the mind-wake path). DISTINCT from the
    # EIGENFORM block above: that is a PERSISTENT anomaly ABSORBED into normal (surprise wrongly FALLS to
    # zero — a false NEGATIVE). Noisy-TV is the COMPLEMENT — irreducible noise NEVER absorbed (surprise
    # wrongly STAYS high — a false POSITIVE). Same missing ingredient (a learnability/reducibility read),
    # opposite error sign. NOT the --conditional explaining-away (handles structure, not stochasticity).
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    trans = {}
    if conditional:
        btypes = [event_type(l) for l in baseline]
        for a, b in zip(btypes, btypes[1:]):
            trans.setdefault(a, Counter())[b] += 1
    def p_cond(prev, cur):
        row = trans.get(prev)
        if row and sum(row.values()) > 0:
            cand = (row.get(cur, 0) + 1) / (sum(row.values()) + V)
            return min(cand, p(cur))        # never less surprising than the marginal floor
        return p(cur)                       # unseen context → marginal back-off
    # score the recent window
    scored = []
    start = len(lines) - len(recent)        # global index of recent[0] (for the predecessor)
    for i, l in enumerate(recent):
        t = event_type(l)
        if conditional:
            prev = event_type(lines[start + i - 1]) if start + i - 1 >= 0 else None
            bits = surprisal(p_cond(prev, t))
        else:
            bits = surprisal(p(t))
        novel = t not in base
        scored.append((bits, t, novel, l))
    scored.sort(reverse=True, key=lambda x: x[0])
    mean_bits = sum(s[0] for s in scored) / len(scored)
    # first-seen entities (categorical novelty): a device MAC newly observed by the
    # PRESENCE sense (~/.mesh/presence.log), never harvested from board prose — a MAC
    # merely *quoted* on the board (e.g. a synthetic test address) is not a device.
    # Split the presence log at the recent board window's start time; a baseline is
    # required, else nothing can be called "first-seen". Only a GLOBALLY-UNIQUE UNICAST
    # MAC is a stable real-world device identity worth flagging as a join: first octet
    # with BOTH the locally-administered bit (0x02) and the multicast bit (0x01) CLEAR.
    # Everything else rotates by design and phantoms into every window — classic
    # randomized BLE (0x02 set) AND BLE resolvable/non-resolvable private addresses that
    # carry the multicast bit (0x01) instead (e.g. 0x71 = a rotating RPA, ruled benign 3×
    # on 2026-06-12, evaded the old 0x02-only test). `& 0x03` catches both; no real OUI
    # device is excluded (real devices are always unicast+global → low 2 bits 0). Residual:
    # an RPA with both low bits clear can still slip — DHCP (mesh-lan-newdevice) is the
    # authoritative join sense; BLE presence is corroborating, not authoritative.
    new_macs = []
    pres = read_lines(PRESENCE)
    if pres and recent:
        t0 = recent[0].split(None, 1)[0]      # ISO-Z timestamps compare lexicographically
        hist = [l for l in pres if l.split(None, 1)[0] < t0]
        cur = [l for l in pres if l.split(None, 1)[0] >= t0]
        if hist:
            ephemeral = lambda m: int(m[:2], 16) & 0x03   # locally-administered OR multicast → not a stable device
            curtext = "\n".join(cur)
            hist_macs = {m.upper() for m in MAC.findall("\n".join(hist))}
            # PROXIMITY gate: a first-seen device is "novel" only if it's actually NEAR — a far BLE
            # blip (a neighbour's device drifting through walls, seen once at -95 dBm) is environmental
            # noise, not a presence event. Evidence (2026-06-12): 465 real non-ephemeral MACs in the
            # log, the bulk -86..-102 dBm seen once; the home's own devices sit at -54..-82. Gate at
            # MESH_NOVELTY_RSSI_MIN (default -85). Degrade safe: a MAC with NO parsed RSSI defaults to
            # the threshold → passes (only KNOWN-far devices are suppressed). DHCP (mesh-lan-newdevice)
            # stays the authoritative LAN-join sense; BLE is corroborating, not authoritative.
            near = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_RSSI_MIN", "-85"))
            best = {}
            for rssi, mac in re.findall(r'(-?\d+)\|([0-9A-Fa-f:]{17})', curtext):
                m = mac.upper(); r = int(rssi)
                if r > best.get(m, -999): best[m] = r
            new_macs = sorted(m for m in {x.upper() for x in MAC.findall(curtext)} - hist_macs
                              if not ephemeral(m) and best.get(m, near) >= near)
    # prior-preference floor: must-attend tags present in the recent window, WHATEVER their surprisal.
    # Kept separate from mean_bits/scored so the surprise MEASUREMENT stays pure (no silent inflation) —
    # this is a parallel, honestly-labelled attend-regardless channel, not a doctored novelty score.
    pref_hits = sorted({t for _, t, _, _ in scored if t in PREF_TAGS})
    # LOCAL-GLOBAL two-timescale deviance (report-only; see the LEVELS header block). GLOBAL baseline =
    # long history `base` (surprisal via p()); LOCAL baseline = the recent window MINUS its tip (the
    # immediate short-timescale context). Classify each DISTINCT type in the tip by the (global,local)
    # deviance pair — the dissociation the single-baseline `scored` cannot express.
    tip = min(LEVELS_TIP, len(recent))
    local_ctx = recent[:-tip] if tip < len(recent) else []
    lbase = Counter(event_type(l) for l in local_ctx)
    lN = sum(lbase.values()) + len(lbase) + 1
    def p_local(t):
        # empty local context → back off to the GLOBAL p (dissociation collapses: local==global).
        return ((lbase.get(t, 0) + 1) / lN) if local_ctx else p(t)
    levels = {}
    for l in recent[-tip:]:
        t = event_type(l)
        if t in levels:
            continue
        gs = surprisal(p(t)); ls = surprisal(p_local(t))
        gdev = gs >= LEVELS_HI; ldev = ls >= LEVELS_HI
        cls = ("REGIME-ONSET" if gdev and not ldev else   # global-deviant, local-standard: rare in history,
                                                          #   already recurring locally → anomaly forming
               "LOCAL-BLIP"   if ldev and not gdev else   # local-deviant, global-standard: routine type absent
                                                          #   from immediate context, reappearing → low wake value
               "BOTH-DEVIANT" if gdev and ldev else       # novel now AND historically
               "BASELINE")
        levels[t] = dict(cls=cls, gbits=round(gs, 2), lbits=round(ls, 2))
    # DETERRITORIALIZATION COEFFICIENT (D&G — see the header block). Split the recent window into an
    # EARLY half F and a LATE half S. For each type whose EARLY-half frequency ESCAPED above the long
    # baseline p(t) (a deterritorializing surge), κ = how much of that escape SURVIVED into the late half:
    #   κ = clamp( (late_freq − base) / (early_escape) , 0, 1 )
    # κ→0  the late half returned toward baseline → the surge was RECAPTURED → RELATIVE (a blip);
    # κ→1  the elevated rate HELD (or rose)        → not recaptured           → ABSOLUTE (a line of flight).
    half = len(recent) // 2
    F = Counter(event_type(l) for l in recent[:half])
    S = Counter(event_type(l) for l in recent[half:])
    nF = sum(F.values()) or 1
    nS = sum(S.values()) or 1
    territory = {}
    for t in set(F) | set(S):
        bp = p(t)                              # the long baseline — the type's territory
        fF = F.get(t, 0) / nF                  # early-half frequency
        fS = S.get(t, 0) / nS                  # late-half frequency
        escape = fF - bp                       # the deterritorializing edge (early)
        if escape <= ESCAPE_MIN:               # no significant escape → not a movement, skip
            continue
        persisted = fS - bp                    # how much of the escape survived the reterritorializing edge
        kappa = max(0.0, min(1.0, persisted / escape))
        territory[t] = dict(cls=("ABSOLUTE" if kappa >= 0.5 else "RELATIVE"),
                            kappa=round(kappa, 2), escape=round(escape, 3),
                            early=round(fF, 3), late=round(fS, 3), base=round(bp, 4))
    # ── BAYESIAN SURPRISE (Itti & Baldi) — belief-UPDATE, not improbability (report-only) ────────────
    # LITERATURE (live review 2026-07-28: predictive processing & the Bayesian brain — a foundational
    # idea this very file applied TOO LOOSELY, a SECOND time). The file's #2 payoff is a SPEND gate
    # ("wake on HIGH novelty") keyed on Shannon surprise −log P (marginal above, or --conditional's
    # −log P(e|prev)). Itti & Baldi's core empirical result is that raw improbability is the WRONG
    # attention signal: what attracts attention is BAYESIAN SURPRISE = KL[posterior‖prior], how much a
    # datum MOVES the observer's model — a quantity that can be ~0 for a very improbable event (it
    # changes no belief) and large for a probable one (it shifts beliefs). (Itti & Baldi, "Bayesian
    # surprise attracts human attention", NIPS 2005 / Vision Research 49(10):1295-1306, 2009; Baldi &
    # Itti, "Of bits and wows: A Bayesian theory of surprise with applications to attention", Neural
    # Networks 23(5), 2010. Still the live workhorse of curiosity/intrinsic-reward: "Curiosity-Driven
    # Exploration via Latent Bayesian Surprise", AAAI 2021; and 2024-25 active-inference exploration,
    # e.g. arXiv:2502.02962. Contrast the Schmidhuber block above, which asks WHICH surprise is worth
    # chasing (reducible vs noise) — this asks whether the surprise MOVES THE MODEL at all.)
    #
    # THE GAP: none of the axes above is Bayesian surprise. The `base` Counter IS already a Dirichlet
    # belief over event types (α = count+1, the same Laplace smoothing p() uses), so the KL of a single
    # observation is closed-form (bayes_bits()). The DISSOCIATION this surfaces on the mesh's own board:
    # a KNOWN-rare type ([incident],[health-fail]) scores ~6-8 Shannon bits EVERY recurrence → the raw
    # SPEND gate re-wakes minds each time — yet after the model has absorbed "rare things happen", the
    # 30th incident moves the belief ~0 (HABITUATED). Its belief-move only rebounds when the RATE shifts.
    # Each type is scored as a fraction of a BRAND-NEW type's belief-move at THIS corpus size (bs_new) —
    # corpus-calibrated, cannot saturate (per the pooled-rank doctrine), never an assumed 0..1 raw bar.
    # REPORT-ONLY / advisory, exactly like --levels/--territory/--independence: it does NOT replace the
    # Shannon SPEND gate nor the dark-room must-attend floor (a chronic critical condition must stay
    # attended even once its belief-move habituates — the two are complementary, not substitutes). It
    # names WHICH wakes raw surprisal over-pays; whether to skip one stays with the consumer.
    A_conc = N                                     # Dirichlet concentration = the smoothing p() already uses
    bs_new = bayes_bits(1.0, A_conc)               # reference: a brand-new type's belief-move at this corpus size
    bayesian = {}
    for t in {event_type(l) for l in recent}:
        alpha_t = base.get(t, 0) + 1.0
        bb = bayes_bits(alpha_t, A_conc)
        sb = surprisal(p(t))
        frac = (bb / bs_new) if bs_new > 0 else 0.0
        cls = ("MODEL-MOVING" if frac >= BAYES_FRAC else      # belief moves ≥ half a new type's → genuine attend
               "HABITUATED"   if sb >= LEVELS_HI else         # HIGH Shannon but belief no longer moves → over-wake
               "ROUTINE")                                     # low on both
        bayesian[t] = dict(cls=cls, bbits=round(bb, 3), sbits=round(sb, 2), frac=round(frac, 2))
    bayes_mean = (sum(bayesian[event_type(l)]["bbits"] for l in recent) / len(recent)) if recent else 0.0
    # ── OMISSION / NEGATIVE PREDICTION ERROR — the expected event that DIDN'T fire (report-only) ─────
    # LITERATURE (live review 2026-07-29: predictive processing & the Bayesian brain — what's NEW).
    # The 2023-2026 frontier is not adding another positive-surprise axis; it is asking what a
    # prediction-error signal ACTUALLY REPRESENTS — Furutachi & Hofer, "Rethinking Predictive
    # Processing", Annu. Rev. Neurosci. 49 (2026, 10.1146/annurev-neuro-102124-031410): PE signals that
    # LOOK alike can reflect FUNDAMENTALLY DIFFERENT computations, and the canonical dissociation is the
    # POSITIVE PE (an unexpected input arrived) vs the NEGATIVE / OMISSION PE (a strongly-predicted
    # input FAILED to arrive — the "omission response" / mismatch-negativity to an omitted stimulus,
    # signalled by a distinct cortical population; see also the hierarchical-violation work this file
    # already cites, Jamali et al. eLife 2025, and the omitted-stimulus MMN literature). The dog that
    # did NOT bark carries information; a −log P(x) model over OBSERVED events cannot represent it.
    #
    # THE GAP THIS NAMES: EVERY axis on this file scores an event that is PRESENT in `recent` — marginal
    # surprisal & --conditional (over recent), first-seen entities (present in the current window), the
    # local/global levels (the recent tip), the deterritorialization κ (F/S halves of recent), Bayesian
    # surprise (`{event_type(l) for l in recent}`). Not one iterates the baseline types ABSENT from the
    # window. So a type that was FREQUENT in history and then goes SILENT — a strand that posted daily
    # and stopped, a heartbeat/[health] tag that always recurred and vanished, an [arrivals]/[sense]
    # producer that fell quiet — scores ZERO novelty here (there is no event to score), even though its
    # non-occurrence is highly improbable and highly informative. mesh-reflex-health/mesh-pulse watch
    # PER-ARTIFACT mtime staleness, but that is a set of hard-wired per-organ liveness gates, NOT a
    # unified information-theoretic omission term in the mesh's own attention/wake channel: an operator
    # returning from absence learns from this sense "what was NEW", never "what went SILENT".
    #
    # THE INSTRUMENT (report-only, parallel channel — like /levels /territory /bayesian; does NOT touch
    # mean_bits/scored nor the --threshold wake gate — the SPEND wiring stays the steward's): for each
    # baseline type ABSENT from the recent window, its silence is a Bernoulli(q) no-show across `window`
    # trials, q = its RAW baseline rate. P(zero in N) = (1−q)^N, so the omission surprise is the exact
    # complement of Shannon surprise: obits = −N·log2(1−q). A high-rate type going silent scores high; a
    # rare type's absence scores ~0 (expected). Gated by EXPECTED count N·q ≥ OMIT_MINEXP (default 1 —
    # we only "expect to have seen" a type whose predicted count reaches ~one), so the long Zipfian tail
    # of genuinely-rare types never floods it. DISTINCT from every sibling: the eigenform block is a
    # persistent anomaly ABSORBED (surprise wrongly falls); noisy-TV is irreducible noise NEVER absorbed;
    # LOCAL-BLIP is a type absent from the immediate context but STILL PRESENT elsewhere in the window
    # and reappearing — this is a baseline-frequent type absent from the window ENTIRELY and NOT
    # reappearing. It is the negative-sign complement of the whole file: positive PE = −log P(seen);
    # omission PE = −log P(NOT seen).
    q_total = sum(base.values()) or 1
    recent_types = {event_type(l) for l in recent}
    omissions = {}
    for t, c in base.items():
        if t in recent_types:
            continue                            # it DID fire — a positive axis handles it
        q = c / q_total                         # raw baseline rate (not Laplace-smoothed → a true rate)
        exp = q * window                        # events of this type we'd have EXPECTED in the window
        if exp < OMIT_MINEXP or q >= 1.0:
            continue                            # too rare to expect (or degenerate q=1) → its silence is unsurprising
        obits = -window * math.log2(1.0 - q)    # −log2 P(zero occurrences in `window` Bernoulli(q) trials)
        omissions[t] = dict(obits=round(obits, 2), exp=round(exp, 2), rate=round(q, 4),
                            cls=("SILENT" if obits >= LEVELS_HI else "QUIET"))
    # ── ENACTIVE VALENCE (see the header block) — significance = viability-relevance × CURRENT state ──
    # The one axis that reads the mesh's OWN body-state, not the board. For each viability-relevant
    # (aversive) tag present in the window, significance = base valence × the state multiplier of the
    # current fused posture. All aversive tags share base=1.0 by design — the DISSOCIATION surfaced here
    # is STATE-dependence (same event, different significance by viability), not a ranking among tags.
    posture, posture_age = read_posture()
    smult = STATE_MULT.get(posture, 1.0)          # UNKNOWN (or unmapped posture) → 1.0, state-neutral/honest
    valence = {}
    for t in {event_type(l) for l in recent}:
        if t not in VALENCE_TAGS:
            continue
        sig = 1.0 * smult
        cls = ("AMPLIFIED" if smult > 1.0 else            # threat under already-degraded viability → compounds
               "DAMPED"    if smult < 1.0 else            # (only if a mult<1 posture is configured)
               "STATE-UNKNOWN" if posture == "UNKNOWN" else
               "BASELINE")                                # posture known & neutral (×1.0)
        valence[t] = dict(cls=cls, significance=round(sig, 2), base=1.0,
                          state=posture, mult=round(smult, 2))
    # COMPRESSION PROGRESS reads the FULL board symbol SEQUENCE (a trajectory measure over time,
    # not the recent window like the surprise axes) — see the compression_progress docstring.
    progress = compression_progress([event_type(l) for l in lines]) if len(lines) >= PROGRESS_MIN else \
               dict(cls="INSUFFICIENT", bits_sym=0.0, rho=0.0, delta=0.0, stagnation=len(lines), T=len(lines), Lcurve=[])
    # MATCHED-CONTROL (genuine deviance vs adaptation) — K surrogate baselines, so it is computed ONLY
    # when asked for; the default report path pays nothing. Same predecessors as `scored` above.
    if control:
        _pairs = [(event_type(lines[start + i - 1]) if start + i - 1 >= 0 else None, event_type(l))
                  for i, l in enumerate(recent)]
        ctrl = deviance_control([event_type(l) for l in baseline], _pairs)
    else:
        ctrl = {}
    # WHEN-EXPECTATION (time-locked omission PE) — same opt-in discipline as --control: it walks
    # every board line to build per-type arrival series, so the default report pays nothing.
    whenx = when_expectation(lines, base, recent_types, window) if when else {}
    return dict(when=whenx,
                mean_bits=mean_bits, scored=scored, base=base, conditional=conditional, control=ctrl,
                new_types=[t for _, t, n, _ in scored if n], new_macs=new_macs, pref_hits=pref_hits,
                levels=levels, levels_tip=tip, territory=territory,
                bayesian=bayesian, bayes_mean=bayes_mean, bayes_new_ref=round(bs_new, 3),
                omissions=omissions, valence=valence, posture=posture, posture_age=posture_age,
                progress=progress)

# ── COMPRESSION PROGRESS / STAGNATION LENGTH — interestingness is a DERIVATIVE, not a level ──────────
# LITERATURE (artificial life & open-ended evolution — live review 2026-07-31, angle = a FOUNDATIONAL
# idea applied too loosely). Herrmann & Schmidhuber, "Interestingness as an Inductive Heuristic for
# Future Compression Progress", arXiv:2605.14831 (2026) — the fresh operationalization of Schmidhuber's
# curiosity/creativity theory (compression progress = the driver of interesting-ness). The FOUNDATIONAL
# claim the mesh reads too loosely: EVERY axis above — surprisal, --conditional, --bayesian, --levels,
# --territory — scores a LEVEL of surprise/novelty. But interestingness is NOT novelty and NOT surprise;
# it is COMPRESSION PROGRESS: the improvement in the amortized description length (MDL) of the history as
# more data is ingested. This is the NOISY-TV problem stated exactly: a churny board spewing first-seen
# types (a flapping sensor minting a new device MAC every scan) MAXIMIZES mean surprisal AND maximizes
# --bayesian belief-move (every symbol is genuinely new → the belief moves maximally) — yet it is
# IRREDUCIBLE NOISE with ZERO compression progress. Both surprise axes would PAY the wake; this one says
# skip. The 2026 mechanism is STAGNATION LENGTH (t − m̂): symbols since the last compression breakthrough;
# the paper proves progress-probability decays ~2^-(t-m̂), so the promising object is the one with the
# MOST RECENT progress. DISTINCT from every sibling: --bayesian habituates KNOWN-rare types but is fooled
# by all-NEW-type noise (each moves the belief); --diversity reads marginal shape (order-blind, like
# omega_cycle's target but that lives in mesh-vitality over the genome, not the board); this reads whether
# the board's own symbol SEQUENCE is still becoming more compressible (learnable structure emerging) or
# has stagnated — and if stagnated, whether it's incompressible NOISE or absorbed/MASTERED structure.
#
# THIS EMBODIES THE HELD FIX at :425-459 ("NOISY-TV / REDUCIBLE vs IRREDUCIBLE SURPRISE"). That block
# named exactly this gap on 2026-06-21 and HELD the fix, for one stated reason: "estimating learnability
# needs a multi-window history this single-pass call does not keep." The 2026 paper dissolves that
# objection — compression progress is measured over the FULL symbol SEQUENCE already available in one read
# (the amortized-code-length DERIVATIVE across prefixes), so no persisted multi-window state is needed. The
# block's second caveat (do NOT discount a source that is high-surprise because it is genuinely NEW each
# window vs random) is honoured by construction: the Noisy-TV fixture (all-first-seen types) reads NOISE
# precisely BECAUSE its symbol sequence is INCOMPRESSIBLE, not because it recurs — a genuinely novel-but-
# STRUCTURED emergence reads LEARNING (see --test). Its third caveat (gate nothing until validated — this
# is the mind-wake path) is honoured: report-only, does NOT touch mean_bits or the wake gate (same
# discipline as --levels/--territory/--bayesian/--valence). The behavioral wake-gating the held block
# reserves for the steward stays the steward's; this lands the MEASUREMENT it was blocked on.
def compression_progress(symbols, nseg=None, eps=None):
    """symbols = ordered event-type tokens (the board's own symbol stream). Returns the progress dict.
    A general compressor (zlib) stands in for the MDL code length, as the paper's framing intends.
    Amortized length L(k)=code_bits(prefix k)/k; a BREAKTHROUGH is a checkpoint whose L dropped by ≥
    eps (default PROGRESS_EPS) vs the previous; stagnation = symbols since the last breakthrough (T if
    none). The noise↔mastered split at stagnation uses ρ = compressed/raw bytes (→1 incompressible=NOISE,
    low=MASTERED). eps is a PARAMETER (not only the module global) so --test can drive the RED-first knob."""
    eps = PROGRESS_EPS if eps is None else eps
    T = len(symbols)
    if T < 2:
        return dict(cls="INSUFFICIENT", bits_sym=0.0, rho=0.0, delta=0.0, stagnation=T, T=T, Lcurve=[])
    code, buf = {}, bytearray()
    for s in symbols:                                   # stable byte alphabet by first appearance (tags ≪ 256)
        buf.append(code.setdefault(s, len(code) & 0xFF))
    hdr = len(zlib.compress(b"", 9))                    # fixed zlib header/trailer — an ADDITIVE artifact; subtract it
    def csize(k):
        return max(0, len(zlib.compress(bytes(buf[:k]), 9)) - hdr)
    def L(k):
        return (csize(k) * 8.0 / k) if k > 0 else 0.0
    rho = min(1.0, csize(T) / max(1, T))                # bytes-out / bytes-in: →1 incompressible/noise, low=structured
    nseg = nseg or PROGRESS_NSEG
    ks = sorted(set(max(1, round(T * i / nseg)) for i in range(1, nseg + 1)))
    Ls = [L(k) for k in ks]
    last_bt = 0                                         # index of the last breakthrough checkpoint (0 = none seen)
    for i in range(1, len(Ls)):
        if Ls[i - 1] - Ls[i] >= eps:
            last_bt = i
    stag = T - ks[last_bt] if last_bt else T            # STAGNATION LENGTH in symbols
    delta = round(Ls[-1 - 1] - Ls[-1], 4) if len(Ls) >= 2 else 0.0   # tail progress (last checkpoint step)
    learning = delta >= eps
    if learning:
        cls = "LEARNING"                               # amortized code length still dropping → learnable structure emerging
    elif rho >= PROGRESS_RHO_HI:
        cls = "NOISE"                                  # stagnated & incompressible → Noisy-TV: high surprise, no structure
    else:
        cls = "MASTERED"                               # stagnated & compressible → structure already absorbed
    return dict(cls=cls, bits_sym=round(Ls[-1], 3), rho=round(rho, 3),
                delta=delta, stagnation=stag, T=T, Lcurve=[round(x, 3) for x in Ls])

def diversity(base):
    """Shannon evenness (Pielou's J) of the RAW baseline type distribution — see the
    DIVERSITY docstring block above. Returns (H_bits, evenness 0..1, label). k<2 distinct
    types is trivially a monoculture (evenness undefined, reported as 0/DEGENERATE)."""
    total = sum(base.values())
    k = len(base)
    if k < 2 or total == 0:
        return (0.0, 0.0, "DEGENERATE")
    h = -sum((c / total) * math.log2(c / total) for c in base.values() if c > 0)
    j = h / math.log2(k)
    label = "DEGENERATE" if j < 0.35 else "FLAT" if j > 0.75 else "STRUCTURED"
    return (h, j, label)

# ── COGNITIVE TEMPERING (focusing ↔ diversifying) — the third RR opponent pair ──────────────────────
# LITERATURE (relevance realization & the frame problem — live review 2026-07-30, angle = a RECENT
# result naming a mechanism we do NOT yet embody). Vervaeke's relevance realization is realized by
# THREE nested opponent pairs, not one (Vervaeke, Lillicrap & Richards, "Relevance Realization and the
# Emerging Framework in Cognitive Science", J. Logic & Computation 22(1):79-99, 2012,
# sites.utoronto.ca/jvcourses/jolc.pdf): cognitive PRIORITIZATION (explore↔exploit), cognitive SCOPE
# (general↔specific), and cognitive TEMPERING (focusing↔diversifying) — how CONCENTRATED vs SPREAD the
# agent's finite resources are over its options. The RECENT grounding that makes it operational here:
# Andersen, Miller & Vervaeke, "Predictive processing and relevance realization: exploring convergent
# solutions to the frame problem", Phenom. & Cog. Sci. 24:359-380 (2025, doi:10.1007/s11097-022-09850-6)
# shows this whole tradeoff FAMILY is the tradeoff inherent to PRECISION-WEIGHTING (gain): tempering IS
# the gain knob — high precision/gain NARROWS attention (focus), low gain BROADENS it (diversify) — so
# the balance is not a fixed set-point but tracks AROUSAL, exactly like the explore/exploit edge
# mesh-needs already reads against DEMAND (Vervaeke: the edge MOVES; a midpoint is the misread).
#
# WHAT THE MESH ALREADY HAS vs THIS GAP: explore↔exploit = mesh-needs --balance (demand-edge);
# efficiency↔resiliency = mesh-sensorium --balance; the diametric precision POLE = mesh-correlate
# --posture; and forage-lane concentration = mesh-forage pheromone-entropy. But NONE of them read the
# focus↔diversify balance of the mesh's OWN activity, and — the load-bearing part — none COUPLE that
# balance to arousal. This does: it reuses diversity()'s already-calibrated evenness bands (the
# diversify axis) and read_posture()'s honest-fused NOMINAL/WATCH/ALERT (the arousal axis), and emits
# the SAME edge-not-midpoint verdict shape as mesh-needs' _demand_verdict. Report-only.
def _tempering_verdict(j, posture):
    """Pure arousal×evenness edge verdict (tested directly, like mesh-needs' _demand_verdict).
    j = Pielou evenness of activity types (low=FOCUSED, high=DIFFUSE); posture = fused arousal.
    Returns (token, note). Reuses diversity()'s OWN bands (0.35 / 0.75) so there is no second
    magic constant to rot. UNKNOWN/neutral posture → pole named, NO edge verdict (honest)."""
    pole = "FOCUSED" if j < 0.35 else "DIFFUSE" if j > 0.75 else "TEMPERED"
    aroused = posture in ("ALERT", "WATCH")            # high arousal = gain should be UP = narrow
    if posture == "UNKNOWN":
        return ("POSTURE-UNKNOWN", f"{pole}; no/stale .situation.state — arousal unknown, edge not judged")
    if pole == "TEMPERED":
        return ("TEMPERED", "mid evenness — neither pole; balance held")
    if pole == "FOCUSED" and aroused:
        return ("NARROWED-TO-THREAT", f"focus under {posture} — RR-CORRECT (gain up, attention narrows to the threat)")
    if pole == "FOCUSED" and not aroused:
        return ("FIXATION", f"focus under {posture} — FAULT: narrowed with no arousal to justify it (tempering's dark-room)")
    if pole == "DIFFUSE" and aroused:
        return ("SCATTERED", f"spread under {posture} — SUBOPTIMAL: RR says gain should rise and narrow, not hedge broad")
    return ("EXPLORING", f"spread under {posture} — RR-CORRECT (nothing presses; broad hedging is the right edge)")

def fmt(a):
    out = []
    pref = a.get('pref_hits') or []
    mode = "contextual prediction-error" if a.get('conditional') else "marginal surprise"
    verdict = ('NOVEL — worth a look' if a['mean_bits'] >= 4.0
               else ('routine · must-attend present' if pref else 'routine'))
    out.append(f"🔭 mesh-novelty — recent window mean {mode}: {a['mean_bits']:.2f} bits ({verdict})")
    top = [s for s in a['scored'] if s[0] >= 4.0][:5]
    if top:
        out.append("── most surprising recent events ──")
        for bits, t, novel, l in top:
            tagn = f"[{t}]" + (" NEW-TYPE" if novel else "")
            out.append(f"  {bits:4.1f}b {tagn}: {l[:90]}")
    # PRIOR-PREFERENCE FLOOR (dark-room): shown even when the window is "routine" — a chronic critical
    # type has LOW surprise (absorbed) yet must still be attended. Attended regardless of surprise.
    if pref:
        out.append("── must-attend (prior preference — attended regardless of surprise) ──")
        out.append("  " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in pref)
                   + "  (dark-room floor: not explained away even once it becomes routine)")
    if a['new_macs']:
        out.append("── first-seen devices (novel presence) ──")
        for m in a['new_macs'][:5]:
            out.append(f"  + {m}")
    # OMISSION / NEGATIVE PREDICTION ERROR: baseline-frequent types that went SILENT in the window.
    # The complement of "most surprising events" — the surprise of what DIDN'T happen. Report-only.
    silent = sorted(((d['obits'], t, d) for t, d in (a.get('omissions') or {}).items()
                     if d['cls'] == "SILENT"), reverse=True)[:5]
    if silent:
        out.append("── expected-but-SILENT (omission / negative prediction error) ──")
        for obits, t, d in silent:
            out.append(f"  {obits:5.1f}b [{t}] went quiet — expected ~{d['exp']:.1f} this window (rate {d['rate']}), saw 0")
    if not top and not a['new_macs'] and not pref and not silent:
        out.append("  (nothing surprising — the window is routine)")
    return "\n".join(out)

def _edge_decision(prev, mean, topN, min_gap, now):
    """Pure gate for --edge — returns (emit: bool, new_state | None).

    Fires when the novelty picture MATERIALLY changed since the last emit:
    a >±0.5b mean shift (score-band) OR a new entry in the top-5 composition.
    A non-zero min_gap adds a time FLOOR: a real edge inside the gap is held
    silent AND the baseline is left untouched (new_state=None), so the pending
    change still fires once the gap elapses — the floor delays, never swallows.
    This is the throttle the novelty-review cadence wants: a poster adopts
    `mesh-novelty --edge --min-gap 900` and posts only when this emits."""
    if prev:
        prev_top = prev.get("top5", prev.get("top3", []))   # back-compat w/ old state
        prev_mean = prev.get("mean", mean)
        if abs(mean - prev_mean) <= 0.5 and not any(t not in prev_top for t in topN):
            return (False, None)                            # no meaningful change
        if min_gap and (now - prev.get("emit_ts", 0)) < min_gap:
            return (False, None)                            # real edge, rate-floored
    return (True, {"mean": mean, "top5": topN, "emit_ts": now})

def main():
    args = sys.argv[1:]
    if "--test" in args:
        # self-test on a synthetic stream: a flood of routine + one rare event
        global read_lines
        sample = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 50
                  + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [incident] something rare just happened"])
        _orig = read_lines
        read_lines = lambda p: sample if p == CHAT else []
        a = analyse(window=10)
        read_lines = _orig
        ok = a and any(t == "incident" for _, t, _, _ in a["scored"][:3])
        if not ok:
            print("smoke-test: FAIL (rare event not ranked surprising)"); sys.exit(1)
        # --edge gate: a real edge inside the min-gap is floored; the SAME edge after the
        # gap emits; an unchanged window is silent regardless of gap; back-compat top3 state.
        base = {"mean": 4.0, "top5": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e"], "emit_ts": 1000}
        e_floor, _  = _edge_decision(base, 4.0, ["z", "b", "c", "d", "e"], 900, 1100)  # edge, 100s<900
        e_after, st = _edge_decision(base, 4.0, ["z", "b", "c", "d", "e"], 900, 2000)  # edge, 1000s>900
        e_same, _   = _edge_decision(base, 4.0, ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e"],   0, 9999)  # no change
        e_band, _   = _edge_decision(base, 4.7, ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e"],   0, 9999)  # +0.7b score-band
        e_compat, _ = _edge_decision({"mean": 4.0, "top3": ["a", "b", "c"]}, 4.0, ["z", "b", "c", "d", "e"], 0, 1)
        if not (e_floor is False and e_after is True and st.get("emit_ts") == 2000
                and e_same is False and e_band is True and e_compat is True):
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (edge gate floor={e_floor} after={e_after} "
                  f"same={e_same} band={e_band} compat={e_compat})"); sys.exit(1)
        # --conditional (predictive-coding) gate: baseline = STRICT taking↔done alternation, then a
        # SECOND [done] in a row appended. [done] is a marginally-common type (≈1 bit) so MARGINAL
        # scoring shrugs; but done-after-done never happens in context, so CONTEXTUAL scoring flags
        # it as high prediction error ("explaining away" the predictable, surfacing the unexpected).
        sample2 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [taking] x", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 30
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"])
        read_lines = lambda p: sample2 if p == CHAT else []
        ac = analyse(window=10, conditional=True)
        am = analyse(window=10, conditional=False)
        read_lines = _orig
        ok2 = (ac and am and ac["scored"][0][1] == "done" and ac["scored"][0][0] > 3.0
               and am["scored"][0][0] < 2.0 and ac["mean_bits"] > am["mean_bits"])
        if not ok2:
            ct = ac["scored"][0] if ac else None; mt = am["scored"][0] if am else None
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (conditional gate: cond_top={ct} marg_top={mt})"); sys.exit(1)
        # --diversity: a monoculture (one type) is DEGENERATE; a Zipfian skew (few common +
        # long tail, like the real board) is STRUCTURED; a uniform spread is FLAT.
        mono = Counter({"done": 40})
        zipfy = Counter({"done": 50, "idle": 25, "taking": 12, "fyi": 6, "sense": 3, "incident": 1, "gap": 1})
        flat = Counter({t: 10 for t in "abcdefgh"})
        h_m, j_m, l_m = diversity(mono)
        h_z, j_z, l_z = diversity(zipfy)
        h_f, j_f, l_f = diversity(flat)
        ok3 = (l_m == "DEGENERATE" and j_m == 0.0 and l_z == "STRUCTURED" and l_f == "FLAT"
               and j_z < j_f)
        if not ok3:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (diversity mono={l_m}/{j_m:.2f} zipf={l_z}/{j_z:.2f} flat={l_f}/{j_f:.2f})")
            sys.exit(1)
        # COGNITIVE TEMPERING (focusing↔diversifying, arousal-coupled): assert every cell of the
        # evenness×arousal matrix, so the edge-not-midpoint verdict is real. RED-first knobs below.
        tv = {
            ("focus_alert",  _tempering_verdict(0.20, "ALERT")[0]):   "NARROWED-TO-THREAT",
            ("focus_nom",    _tempering_verdict(0.20, "NOMINAL")[0]): "FIXATION",
            ("diffuse_alert",_tempering_verdict(0.90, "ALERT")[0]):   "SCATTERED",
            ("diffuse_nom",  _tempering_verdict(0.90, "NOMINAL")[0]): "EXPLORING",
            ("mid",          _tempering_verdict(0.55, "ALERT")[0]):   "TEMPERED",
            ("unknown",      _tempering_verdict(0.20, "UNKNOWN")[0]): "POSTURE-UNKNOWN",
        }
        bad_t = [f"{k[0]}={k[1]}(want {want})" for k, want in tv.items() if k[1] != want]
        # FALSIFIER: FIXATION (the fault) must be REACHABLE and must NOT fire when arousal justifies focus —
        # i.e. the same low evenness under ALERT is NOT a fault. A verdict that can never separate them is vacuous.
        if _tempering_verdict(0.20, "NOMINAL")[0] == _tempering_verdict(0.20, "ALERT")[0]:
            bad_t.append("arousal-blind (focus verdict ignores posture)")
        if bad_t:
            print("smoke-test: FAIL (tempering verdict: " + " ".join(bad_t) + ")"); sys.exit(1)
        # PRIOR-PREFERENCE FLOOR (dark-room): a chronic [health-fail] is ABSORBED into the baseline
        # (low marginal surprise, NOT a new type) — proving the boiling-frog failure is real — yet it
        # must still be surfaced as must-attend. Asserts BOTH: the absorption, and the floor catching it.
        sample4 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [health-fail] node down"] * 30)
        read_lines = lambda p: sample4 if p == CHAT else []
        ap = analyse(window=10)
        read_lines = _orig
        hf = [s for s in ap["scored"] if s[1] == "health-fail"]
        absorbed = bool(hf) and hf[0][0] < 4.0 and "health-fail" not in ap["new_types"]
        # NOTE the RED-first knob: MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_TAGS="" empties PREF_TAGS → pref_hits empty → FAIL.
        ok4 = absorbed and "health-fail" in ap.get("pref_hits", [])
        if not ok4:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (prior-preference floor: absorbed={absorbed} "
                  f"pref_hits={ap.get('pref_hits')} hf_bits={hf[0][0] if hf else None})"); sys.exit(1)
        # LOCAL-GLOBAL two-timescale deviance: build a stream where the SAME single-baseline surprisal
        # cannot tell two recent-tip types apart, but the local/global split can.
        #   [deploy] is ABSENT from long history yet fills the immediate local context (recurring) →
        #            global-deviant + local-standard → REGIME-ONSET (an anomaly forming, pre-absorption).
        #   [done]  is COMMON in long history but ABSENT from the immediate local context, reappearing at
        #            the tip → global-standard + local-deviant → LOCAL-BLIP (routine oddball, low wake).
        # RED-first knob: MESH_NOVELTY_LEVELS_TIP>=window empties the LOCAL context → p_local backs off to
        # the GLOBAL p → local==global → deploy reads BOTH-DEVIANT and done reads BASELINE → this FAILS.
        sample5 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 60
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [deploy] a"] * 20
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [deploy] a", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x",
                      "00:00:00Z a@n :: [deploy] a", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x",
                      "00:00:00Z a@n :: [deploy] a"])
        read_lines = lambda p: sample5 if p == CHAT else []
        al = analyse(window=25)
        read_lines = _orig
        lv = (al or {}).get("levels", {})
        ok5 = (lv.get("deploy", {}).get("cls") == "REGIME-ONSET"
               and lv.get("done", {}).get("cls") == "LOCAL-BLIP")
        if not ok5:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (local-global levels: deploy={lv.get('deploy')} "
                  f"done={lv.get('done')} — want deploy=REGIME-ONSET, done=LOCAL-BLIP)"); sys.exit(1)
        # DETERRITORIALIZATION COEFFICIENT (D&G): two types both SURGE in the early half of the window
        # (both absent from the long baseline → both escape), but they differ in RECAPTURE:
        #   [flight] persists at the same elevated rate into the LATE half → not recaptured → ABSOLUTE.
        #   [blip]   vanishes in the late half (board returns toward baseline) → recaptured → RELATIVE.
        # Magnitude alone cannot tell them apart (identical early surprise); only the late-half recapture
        # read does. RED-first knob: MESH_NOVELTY_ESCAPE_MIN=1.0 makes NO surge clear the escape floor →
        # territory empties → both assertions go red.
        sample6 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 80
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [flight] a", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [blip] b"] * 5   # early half: both surge
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [flight] a", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 5)  # late half: flight holds, blip gone
        read_lines = lambda p: sample6 if p == CHAT else []
        at = analyse(window=20)
        read_lines = _orig
        tv = (at or {}).get("territory", {})
        ok6 = (tv.get("flight", {}).get("cls") == "ABSOLUTE"
               and tv.get("blip", {}).get("cls") == "RELATIVE"
               and tv["flight"]["kappa"] > tv["blip"]["kappa"])
        if not ok6:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (deterritorialization: flight={tv.get('flight')} "
                  f"blip={tv.get('blip')} — want flight=ABSOLUTE, blip=RELATIVE)"); sys.exit(1)
        # BAYESIAN SURPRISE (Itti & Baldi): the dissociation Shannon surprise cannot express. A stream
        # where [incident] is KNOWN-rare (30 in the long baseline → HIGH Shannon every recurrence, but
        # the belief has absorbed "rare things happen" → ~0 belief-move → HABITUATED) vs [surge], a
        # brand-new type at the tip (first sighting → maximal belief-move → MODEL-MOVING). BOTH are
        # high-Shannon; only Bayesian surprise separates the wasted wake from the genuine one.
        # RED-first knob: replacing bayes_bits() with surprisal() (belief-move → improbability) makes
        # incident's frac clear BAYES_FRAC → it reads MODEL-MOVING → this FAILS. Plus a digamma anchor.
        sample7 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 2000
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [incident] known rare"] * 30
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 6
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [incident] recurs",
                      "00:00:00Z a@n :: [surge] never seen before"])
        read_lines = lambda p: sample7 if p == CHAT else []
        ab = analyse(window=10)
        read_lines = _orig
        bv = (ab or {}).get("bayesian", {})
        inc = bv.get("incident", {}); sur = bv.get("surge", {})
        dg1 = _digamma(1.0); dg2 = _digamma(2.0)
        ok7 = (inc.get("cls") == "HABITUATED" and sur.get("cls") == "MODEL-MOVING"
               and inc.get("sbits", 0) >= LEVELS_HI                       # incident IS high Shannon surprise
               and sur.get("bbits", 0) > inc.get("bbits", 9) * 3          # yet the new type moves belief far more
               and abs(dg1 - (-0.5772156649)) < 1e-3                      # ψ(1) = −γ  (formula anchor)
               and abs(dg2 - 0.4227843351) < 1e-3)                       # ψ(2) = 1−γ
        if not ok7:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (bayesian surprise: incident={inc} surge={sur} "
                  f"dg1={dg1:.5f} dg2={dg2:.5f} — want incident=HABITUATED hi-Shannon, "
                  f"surge=MODEL-MOVING, bbits(surge)>3·bbits(incident))"); sys.exit(1)
        # OMISSION / NEGATIVE PREDICTION ERROR: a type FREQUENT in the baseline that goes SILENT in the
        # recent window is a high-information non-event, invisible to every positive (present-event) axis
        # above. [beacon] fills half the long baseline (rate ≈0.5) then vanishes from the window; [done]
        # is present in the window → NOT an omission. Only the omission axis scores the silence.
        # RED-first knob: MESH_NOVELTY_OMIT_MINEXP=999 makes NO type's expected count clear the floor →
        # omissions empties → beacon's silence goes unscored → this FAILS.
        sample8 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [beacon] ping", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 60
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 10)
        read_lines = lambda p: sample8 if p == CHAT else []
        ao = analyse(window=10)
        read_lines = _orig
        om = (ao or {}).get("omissions", {})
        bk = om.get("beacon", {})
        ok8 = (bk.get("cls") == "SILENT" and bk.get("obits", 0) >= LEVELS_HI
               and bk.get("exp", 0) >= OMIT_MINEXP and "done" not in om)   # done fired → excluded
        if not ok8:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (omission PE: beacon={bk} done_in_om={'done' in om} "
                  f"— want beacon=SILENT hi-obits with exp≥{OMIT_MINEXP}, done excluded)"); sys.exit(1)
        # ENACTIVE VALENCE (state-DEPENDENT significance): the SAME [gap] event carries HIGHER
        # significance when the mesh's fused posture is ALERT than when NOMINAL — the enactive turn from
        # INFORMATION (board-only, what every other axis scores) to SIGNIFICANCE (board × current
        # viability). posture is injected via MESH_NOVELTY_POSTURE so the test needs no .situation.state.
        # RED-first knob: run `MESH_NOVELTY_STATE_MULT="NOMINAL:1,WATCH:1,ALERT:1" mesh-novelty --test`
        # → ALERT and NOMINAL multipliers collapse to equal → the significance no longer differs by
        # state → the `sig_alert > sig_nom` assertion goes RED (proving the state-dependence is real).
        sampleV = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 40
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [gap] a strand went silent"])
        read_lines = lambda p: sampleV if p == CHAT else []
        os.environ["MESH_NOVELTY_POSTURE"] = "ALERT";   av_alert = analyse(window=10)
        os.environ["MESH_NOVELTY_POSTURE"] = "NOMINAL"; av_nom = analyse(window=10)
        os.environ["MESH_NOVELTY_POSTURE"] = "UNKNOWN"; av_unk = analyse(window=10)   # unmapped/absent posture
        os.environ.pop("MESH_NOVELTY_POSTURE", None)
        read_lines = _orig
        va = (av_alert or {}).get("valence", {}).get("gap", {})
        vn = (av_nom or {}).get("valence", {}).get("gap", {})
        vu = (av_unk or {}).get("valence", {}).get("gap", {})
        # gap must be scored (it's an aversive/viability tag); benign [done] must NOT be (not viability-rel).
        ok9 = (va.get("cls") == "AMPLIFIED" and vn.get("cls") == "BASELINE"
               and va.get("significance", 0) > vn.get("significance", 9)      # SAME event, higher sig under ALERT
               and vu.get("cls") == "STATE-UNKNOWN" and vu.get("mult") == 1.0  # honest: unknown → state-neutral
               and "done" not in (av_alert or {}).get("valence", {}))          # non-viability tag not valenced
        if not ok9:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (enactive valence: gap@ALERT={va} gap@NOMINAL={vn} gap@UNKNOWN={vu} "
                  f"done_valenced={'done' in (av_alert or {}).get('valence', {})} — want ALERT>NOMINAL, "
                  f"UNKNOWN state-neutral, [done] unscored)"); sys.exit(1)
        # COMPRESSION PROGRESS / STAGNATION LENGTH (Herrmann & Schmidhuber 2026): interestingness is a
        # DERIVATIVE (compression progress), not a LEVEL of surprise. Three symbol streams, tested on the
        # pure function so the classification is direct (like diversity/_tempering_verdict):
        #   LEARNING  — 40 distinct noise symbols THEN 60 of a tight period-3 pattern: adding the recent
        #               half sharply drops amortized code length at the tail → a fresh breakthrough.
        #   NOISE     — 100 all-distinct first-seen types (permutation): incompressible, ρ→1, no progress —
        #               yet EVERY symbol is novel, so mean surprisal is HIGH (the Noisy-TV over-pay).
        #   MASTERED  — a period-3 pattern × 200 = 600 symbols: highly compressible (low ρ) but the tail
        #               amortized-length drop has fallen below PROGRESS_EPS → stagnated & absorbed.
        learn_syms = [f"n{i}" for i in range(40)] + (["a", "b", "c"] * 20)
        noise_syms = [f"x{i}" for i in range(100)]
        master_syms = (["a", "b", "c"] * 200)
        pl = compression_progress(learn_syms)
        pn = compression_progress(noise_syms)
        pm = compression_progress(master_syms)
        ok_pg = (pl["cls"] == "LEARNING" and pn["cls"] == "NOISE" and pm["cls"] == "MASTERED"
                 and pn["rho"] >= PROGRESS_RHO_HI and pm["rho"] < PROGRESS_RHO_HI
                 and pl["delta"] >= PROGRESS_EPS and pm["delta"] < PROGRESS_EPS)
        if not ok_pg:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (compression progress: learn={pl} noise={pn} master={pm})"); sys.exit(1)
        # THESIS leg — the "applied too loosely" correction, asserted: on the NOISE stream the SURPRISE
        # axes over-pay. mean_bits (raw surprisal) is HIGH (every type first-seen) AND --bayesian reads the
        # tip as MODEL-MOVING (a genuinely new type moves the belief maximally) — both would trip a wake —
        # while compression progress says NOISE (no learnable structure → skip). Surprise ≠ interestingness.
        # NB tags are letter-only (`[a-z][a-z-]*`) — a digit voids the tag → the line parses as _chat.
        _ntag = lambda i: chr(97 + i // 26) + chr(97 + i % 26)                # aa, ab, ... (100 distinct)
        read_lines2 = lambda p: [f"00:00:00Z a@n :: [{_ntag(i)}] first seen" for i in range(100)] if p == CHAT else []
        _orig2 = read_lines; read_lines = read_lines2
        an = analyse(window=10)
        read_lines = _orig2
        bv_n = (an or {}).get("bayesian", {})
        tip_moving = any(d.get("cls") == "MODEL-MOVING" for d in bv_n.values())
        ok_thesis = (an and an["mean_bits"] >= LEVELS_HI and tip_moving
                     and an["progress"]["cls"] == "NOISE")
        if not ok_thesis:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (thesis: noise mean_bits={an['mean_bits'] if an else None} "
                  f"bayesian_model_moving={tip_moving} progress={an['progress']['cls'] if an else None} "
                  f"— want HIGH surprise + belief-move BUT progress=NOISE)"); sys.exit(1)
        # RED-first knob: PROGRESS_EPS huge → NO checkpoint ever clears the breakthrough bar → the LEARNING
        # stream can no longer read LEARNING (the derivative gate is load-bearing, not decorative).
        pl_dead = compression_progress(learn_syms, eps=99.0)
        if pl_dead["cls"] == "LEARNING":
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (progress eps knob: LEARNING survived eps=99 → gate vacuous: {pl_dead})")
            sys.exit(1)
        # ── MATCHED-CONTROL gate (--control): genuine deviance vs adaptation ────────────────────────
        # Three fixtures with the SAME alphabet, differing only in whether a sequential REGULARITY
        # exists to violate. Deterministic (fixed surrogate seed) — these numbers are reproducible.
        def _ctrl(sample, **kw):
            global read_lines
            _o = read_lines
            read_lines = lambda p: sample if p == CHAT else []
            r = analyse(window=10, control=True)
            read_lines = _o
            return (r or {}).get("control", {})
        # A — a REAL regularity (strict taking↔done alternation) + a done-after-done violation.
        ca = _ctrl(sample2)
        # B — the SAME lines order-shuffled: identical marginals, identical adaptational state, NO
        #     regularity. The identical tip event must NOT survive the control.
        _r = random.Random(7); _sh = list(sample2[:-1]); _r.shuffle(_sh)
        cb = _ctrl(_sh + [sample2[-1]])
        # C — THESIS leg: an i.i.d. 3-symbol stream (nothing to violate, by construction). The CLASSIC
        #     --conditional excess is large anyway (sparse Laplace-smoothed rows manufacture bits), yet
        #     nothing is genuine — the mesh's "no genuine intensity MMN".
        _r2 = random.Random(11)
        cc = _ctrl([f"00:00:00Z a@n :: [{t}] x" for t in [_r2.choice("abc") for _ in range(60)]])
        ok_ca = ca.get("done", {}).get("cls") == "GENUINE" and ca["done"]["genuine"] >= 0.3
        ok_cb = cb.get("done", {}).get("cls") != "GENUINE"
        ok_cc = (not any(d["cls"] == "GENUINE" for d in cc.values())
                 and max((d["classic"] for d in cc.values()), default=0) >= 0.4)
        if not (ok_ca and ok_cb and ok_cc):
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (control gate: structured={ca.get('done')} "
                  f"surrogate={cb.get('done')} iid={cc}) — want GENUINE only where a regularity exists")
            sys.exit(1)
        # RED-first knob: α=0 admits no p-value → NOTHING can be GENUINE. If the structured fixture
        # still reads GENUINE the significance test is decorative, not load-bearing.
        _pairs = [(a_, b_) for a_, b_ in zip([event_type(l) for l in sample2[-11:-1]],
                                             [event_type(l) for l in sample2[-10:]])]
        dead = deviance_control([event_type(l) for l in sample2[:-10]], _pairs, alpha=0.0)
        if any(d["cls"] == "GENUINE" for d in dead.values()):
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (control α knob: GENUINE survived α=0 → test vacuous: {dead})")
            sys.exit(1)
        # RESOLUTION gate: a permutation test cannot report p below 1/(K+1). Assert (a) the default path
        # RAISES K until significance is attainable — the structured fixture must still read GENUINE with
        # its p at or under α_eff — and (b) a K pinned too low to resolve says UNDERPOWERED, never a null
        # verdict the instrument could not have refuted. Caught on the first LIVE run (17 types, K=200 →
        # floor 0.005 > α_eff 0.0029 → GENUINE unreachable, every type read ADAPTATION).
        res_ok = ca["done"]["p"] <= ca["done"]["alpha_eff"] and ca["done"]["k"] >= 1 / ca["done"]["alpha_eff"] - 1
        weak = deviance_control([event_type(l) for l in sample2[:-10]], _pairs, K=3, kmax=3, alpha=0.05)
        weak_ok = weak.get("done", {}).get("cls") == "UNDERPOWERED"
        if not (res_ok and weak_ok):
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (control resolution: structured={ca['done']} pinned-K3={weak.get('done')}"
                  " — want K auto-raised so GENUINE is attainable, and UNDERPOWERED when it is not)")
            sys.exit(1)
        # ── WHEN-EXPECTATION gate (--when): a learned "when", not a rate ────────────────────────
        # Every number below is a fixed-epoch construction — no RNG, no wallclock (the axis reads
        # the TAPE's last stamp as `now`), so these assertions are reproducible on any node at any
        # hour. Six legs, each the red for a different mutation; see the mutants noted per leg.
        _T0 = 1750000000
        def _wl(tag, ep):
            return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(int(ep))) + f"  a@n  ::  [{tag}] x"
        # FIXTURE A — a REGULAR producer 1.5 intervals overdue, among enough other traffic that its
        # RATE is too low for the count axis to expect one this window. Plus a 3-interval type (below
        # the fit floor), a REGULAR type with only 7 intervals (fit screams, sample cannot resolve),
        # and a type whose last arrival IS `now`.
        _now_a = _T0 + 10500
        _fa  = [_wl("beat", _T0 + i * 600) for i in range(17)]                  # 16 iv, all 600s, CV=0
        _fa += [_wl("rare", _T0 - 100000 + i * 3600) for i in range(8)]         # 7 iv → ceiling 3.0b
        _fa += [_wl("few",  _T0 + i * 900) for i in range(4)]                   # 3 iv → below the floor
        _fa += [_wl("fresh", _now_a - i * 700) for i in range(20)]              # last arrival == now
        _fa += [_wl("filler", _T0 + i * 40) for i in range(250)]                # dilute beat's RATE
        _fa += [_wl("tip", _now_a)]
        _ba = Counter(event_type(l) for l in _fa)
        wa = when_expectation(_fa, _ba, set(), 40)
        beat, rare, few, fresh = wa.get("beat", {}), wa.get("rare", {}), wa.get("few", {}), wa.get("fresh", {})
        # MUTANTS, all run from a scratch copy and each SEEN red, with the leg it actually kills
        # (a mutant that goes red on a different leg than the one it was written for is not evidence
        # for that leg — [[a-mutant-can-go-red-for-the-wrong-reason]]):
        #   M1 k pinned to 1 (the memoryless law the count axis assumes) ......... W1, W3
        #   M2 cons = wbits (drop the conservative min over the two estimators) .. W5, W6
        #   M3 dt measured from times[0] instead of times[-1] .................... W3(W4), W5
        #   M4 MESH_NOVELTY_WHEN_MINIV=0 ......................................... W2
        #   M5 empirical survival without the +1 ................................. W6
        #   M6 _gammq returns 1−Q ................................................ W1, W3
        #   M7 the regularity classifier pinned off REGULAR ...................... W1
        #   M8 `when` computed unconditionally in analyse() (not opt-in) ......... W8
        #   M9 the `ceiling < hi` refusal branch removed ......................... W3 (alone)
        # W1 the load-bearing leg: a REGULAR producer 1.5 mean-intervals late is SILENT under its own
        #    fitted clock, and the count axis is quiet about it. Under M1 the same producer reads
        #    QUIET at 2.2b — the exact bit of the finding, isolated.
        okw1 = (beat.get("cls") == "SILENT" and beat.get("reg") == "REGULAR"
                and beat.get("agree") == "UNDER-CALLED" and beat.get("obits", 9) < LEVELS_HI)
        # W2 the fit floor is load-bearing (M4). Asserted here AND as the knob leg W7 below.
        okw2 = few.get("cls") == "UNSCORABLE" and few.get("n_iv") == 3
        # W3 the RESOLUTION leg — the whole reason for the second estimator. The Gamma fitted to 7
        #    intervals of a perfectly-regular producer 23× overdue reports a manufactured number
        #    (>50b); the distribution-free ceiling log2(8)=3.0b sits under the 4b bar, so the verdict
        #    must REFUSE. M9 removes exactly that refusal and nothing else, and this is the only leg
        #    it kills. NOTE the near-miss: M2 (dropping the empirical leg) does NOT kill this one —
        #    the refusal keys on the CEILING, which survives M2 — so W3 needed its own mutant.
        okw3 = (rare.get("cls") == "UNDERPOWERED" and rare.get("wbits", 0) > 50
                and rare.get("ceiling") == round(math.log2(8), 2) and rare.get("agree") is None)
        # W4 Δt is measured from the type's LAST arrival, not from the tape's start (M3) — `fresh`
        #    last posted AT `now`, so it must read exactly 0 overdue.
        okw4 = fresh.get("cls") == "QUIET" and fresh.get("dt") == 0.0 and fresh.get("cons") == 0.0
        # W6 the +1 in the empirical survival is what makes it a BOUND: no scored type may ever exceed
        #    its own ceiling (M5, M2). Without it, a type overdue past every observed interval has a
        #    zero-count numerator and the conservative bits run away past the resolution.
        okw6 = all(d["cons"] <= d["ceiling"] + 1e-9 for d in wa.values() if d["cls"] != "UNSCORABLE")
        # FIXTURE B — the OTHER direction. A BURSTY producer (clusters of 12, ~1080s between clusters)
        # sitting in an ordinary 900s inter-cluster gap. Its RATE is high, so the count axis calls it
        # SILENT; its own clock says this gap is unremarkable.
        _fb, _bt = [], _T0
        for c in range(20):
            for j in range(12):
                _fb.append(_wl("burst", _bt + c * 1200 + j * 5))
        _last_b = _T0 + 19 * 1200 + 11 * 5
        _fb += [_wl("filler", _T0 + i * 300) for i in range(30)] + [_wl("tip", _last_b + 900)]
        _bb = Counter(event_type(l) for l in _fb)
        wb = when_expectation(_fb, _bb, set(), 40)
        burst = wb.get("burst", {})
        # W5 the other direction, and the leg M2 kills: keep only the parametric estimate and this
        #    ordinary inter-cluster gap clears the bar at 4.06b → burst flips to SILENT/AGREE, i.e.
        #    the count axis's false alarm is reproduced instead of contradicted.
        okw5 = (burst.get("cls") == "QUIET" and burst.get("reg") == "BURSTY"
                and burst.get("agree") == "OVER-CALLED" and burst.get("ceiling", 0) >= LEVELS_HI)
        # W7 RED-first knob: with the floor removed the 3-interval type MUST become scorable. If it
        #    stays UNSCORABLE the floor in W2 was never doing the work.
        okw7 = when_expectation(_fa, _ba, set(), 40, miniv=0).get("few", {}).get("cls") != "UNSCORABLE"
        if not (okw1 and okw2 and okw3 and okw4 and okw5 and okw6 and okw7):
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (when-expectation: W1 regular-under-called={okw1} ({beat}) | "
                  f"W2 fit-floor={okw2} | W3 resolution-refusal={okw3} ({rare}) | W4 dt-from-last={okw4} | "
                  f"W5 bursty-over-called={okw5} ({burst}) | W6 cons<=ceiling={okw6} | W7 floor-knob={okw7})")
            sys.exit(1)
        # W8 wiring: the axis is OPT-IN (analyse pays nothing by default) and reaches the dict.
        read_lines = lambda p: _fa if p == CHAT else []
        _aw, _ao2 = analyse(window=40, when=True), analyse(window=40, when=False)
        read_lines = _orig
        if not ((_aw or {}).get("when") and (_ao2 or {}).get("when") == {}):
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (when wiring: on={bool((_aw or {}).get('when'))} "
                  f"off={(_ao2 or {}).get('when')} — want populated only with when=True)"); sys.exit(1)
        # ── FEATURE-SPECIFIC PREDICTION ERROR (--features) ───────────────────────────────────────
        # The fixture is built so the two levels DISAGREE by construction: 60 one-off organ markers
        # (rare FORM, the commonest ROLE after [fyi]) against a [done] that is a common form doing a
        # rare coordination act. If the levels were redundant, no leg below could pass.
        def _fl(i, mark, win="w1"):
            return f"2026-08-18T{i//3600:02d}:{(i//60)%60:02d}:{i%60:02d}Z  {win}@h  ::  [{mark}] x"
        fx, i = [], 0
        for _ in range(60):
            fx.append(_fl(i, "fyi")); i += 1
        for k in range(120):          # the board's real shape: organ markers are the plurality ROLE
            fx.append(_fl(i, "s%03d" % k)); i += 1
        for _ in range(20):
            fx.append(_fl(i, "done")); i += 1
        fx += [_fl(i, "zzz-new"), _fl(i + 1, "done"), _fl(i + 2, "fyi")]
        ft = features(fx, window=3, tail=len(fx))
        if ft is None:
            print("smoke-test: FAIL (features: fixture of %d lines rendered n/a)" % len(fx)); sys.exit(1)
        r_new, r_done, r_fyi = ft["rows"]
        # F1 a never-seen MARKER from the commonest role is FORM-dominant — surface-only novelty.
        okf1 = r_new["dom"] == "form" and r_new["n"]["form"] > r_new["n"]["role"]
        # F2 a common marker doing a rare ACT is ROLE-dominant — the direction event_type() cannot see.
        okf2 = r_done["dom"] == "role" and r_done["n"]["role"] > r_done["n"]["form"]
        # F3 THE MUTATION GATE: [done] is the SAME event on both levels, and its RAW surprisal is
        #    HIGHER on form than on role — the opposite of the verdict. F2 can therefore only pass
        #    because each level is divided by its OWN entropy. Delete the /H in nb() and the
        #    dominance INVERTS: F2 and F3 both go RED. (Verified red-then-green this session.)
        hb = {lv: ft["levels"][lv]["h_bits"] for lv in FEAT_LEVELS}
        raw = {lv: r_done["n"][lv] * hb[lv] for lv in ("form", "role")}
        okf3 = (raw["form"] > raw["role"]                       # raw says FORM
                and r_done["n"]["role"] > r_done["n"]["form"]   # normalized says ROLE
                and hb["form"] > 2 * hb["role"])
        # F4 the levels are measurably NON-redundant on the fixture (and here, opposed).
        okf4 = ft["corr"]["form~role"] is not None and ft["corr"]["form~role"] < 0
        # F5 the LOW gate and the HIGH gate pick different events at all.
        okf5 = ft["gate"]["overlap"] < ft["gate"]["k"]
        # F6 an unremarkable event is dominant on NO level by much — the axis is not always-on.
        okf6 = r_fyi["spread"] < r_new["spread"] and r_fyi["spread"] < r_done["spread"]
        # F7 HONEST N/A: too little board renders None, never a "levels agree" (fabricated calm).
        okf7 = features(fx[:FEAT_MIN], window=3) is None
        if not (okf1 and okf2 and okf3 and okf4 and okf5 and okf6 and okf7):
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (features: F1 form-dominant={okf1} ({r_new['dom']}) | "
                  f"F2 role-dominant={okf2} ({r_done['dom']}) | F3 raw-bits-tie/own-entropy={okf3} "
                  f"(raw {raw['form']:.2f} vs {raw['role']:.2f}, H {hb['form']:.2f} vs {hb['role']:.2f}) | "
                  f"F4 levels-non-redundant={okf4} (r={ft['corr']['form~role']}) | "
                  f"F5 gates-differ={okf5} | F6 quiet-event-flat={okf6} | F7 honest-na={okf7})")
            sys.exit(1)
        # ── UNCERTAINTY-DRIVEN vs ERROR-DRIVEN BOUNDARIES (--uncertainty) ─────────────────────────
        # The fixture holds two contexts that DISAGREE by construction, which is the whole claim:
        #   [flat] → 8 successors uniformly  → a SHARP error signal is impossible there (every
        #            successor is ordinary) while the model itself carries no prediction at all;
        #   [det]  → always [dee]            → zero uncertainty, and a violation of it is pure error.
        # Plus a never-seen context (NO-MODEL) and a 3-observation context (UNDERPOWERED), the two
        # ways a row's maximal smoothed entropy is the INSTRUMENT's blankness rather than the board's.
        UL = ["sa", "sb", "sc", "sd", "se", "sf", "sg", "sh"]
        useq = []
        for _u in range(24):
            _k = _u % 8
            useq += ["det", "dee", "flat", UL[_k], UL[_k], UL[_k], UL[(_k + 3) % 8]]
        useq += ["rare", "sa", "rare", "sa", "rare", "sa"]      # n=3 context → UNDERPOWERED
        urec = ["flat", UL[0], "det", "zzz", "qqq", "rare", "sa", "det"]
        ufx = [f"2026-08-20T00:00:{i % 60:02d}Z  w@h  ::  [{m}] x"
               for i, m in enumerate(useq + urec)]
        UW = len(urec)
        ub = uncertainty_boundaries(ufx, window=UW)
        if ub is None:
            print("smoke-test: FAIL (uncertainty: fixture of %d lines rendered n/a)" % len(ufx))
            sys.exit(1)
        ur = {r["i"]: r for r in ub["rows"]}
        barU, barE = ub["bar_u"], ub["bar_e"]
        # U1 the sharp context is PREDICTABLE and its expected successor fires NEITHER signal.
        oku1 = ur[3]["cons"] == 0.0 and ur[2]["cls"] in ("-", "ERROR-DRIVEN")
        # U2 THE CLAIM: a flat context with an ORDINARY successor. The error axis is SILENT
        #    (bits < the error bar — no mode in this file fires) and the boundary is still called.
        oku2 = ur[1]["cls"] == "UNCERTAINTY-DRIVEN" and ur[1]["bits"] < barE and ur[1]["cons"] >= barU
        # U3 the mirror: a sharp context violated is ERROR-DRIVEN with LOW uncertainty.
        oku3 = ur[3]["cls"] == "ERROR-DRIVEN" and ur[3]["bits"] >= barE and ur[3]["cons"] < barU
        # U4 NO-MODEL refusal is LOAD-BEARING: that row's smoothed entropy is over the bar, so
        #    without the n==0 refusal a never-learned context would be reported as "uncertain" —
        #    the instrument's own blankness read as a property of the board.
        oku4 = ur[4]["cls"] == "NO-MODEL" and ur[4]["cons"] is None and ur[4]["h_smooth"] >= barU
        # U5 UNDERPOWERED refusal, likewise load-bearing in the OTHER direction: 3 observations
        #    cannot demonstrate either predictability or its absence (ceiling under the bar).
        oku5 = (ur[6]["cls"] == "UNDERPOWERED" and ur[6]["n"] < ub["minsup"]
                and ur[6]["ceiling"] < barU and ur[6]["h_smooth"] >= barU)
        # U6 the CONSERVATIVE MIN is load-bearing: row [sa] sits OVER the bar on the smoothed leg
        #    and UNDER it on the bias-corrected empirical leg. Take h_smooth alone (the number a
        #    consumer of the model would naively use) and this row is called uncertain on prior mass.
        oku6 = (ur[2]["h_smooth"] >= barU and ur[2]["cons"] < barU
                and ur[1]["h_smooth"] > ur[1]["h_mm"] and ur[1]["cons"] == ur[1]["h_mm"])
        # U7 PROACTIVE, demonstrated: `next` is a function of the LAST TYPE and the baseline only.
        #    Replace every recent line except the last with different ordinary events — the baseline
        #    is untouched, no successor of [det] exists anywhere — and the verdict must not move.
        ualt = ufx[:-UW] + [f"2026-08-20T00:01:{i:02d}Z  w@h  ::  [dee] x" for i in range(UW - 1)] \
               + [ufx[-1]]
        ub2 = uncertainty_boundaries(ualt, window=UW)
        oku7 = (ub["next"]["ctx"] == "det" and ub2 is not None and ub2["next"] == ub["next"]
                and ub["next"]["cls"] == "PREDICTIVE")
        # U8 HONEST N/A: too little board renders None, never an empty "no boundaries".
        oku8 = uncertainty_boundaries(ufx[:UNC_MINBASE], window=UW) is None
        # U9 the two signals are non-redundant on the fixture — both exclusive classes occur.
        oku9 = (ub["counts"].get("ERROR-DRIVEN", 0) >= 1
                and ub["counts"].get("UNCERTAINTY-DRIVEN", 0) >= 1)
        # U10 the ERROR leg IS --conditional's number, not a second opinion: same events, same bits.
        _o = read_lines
        read_lines = lambda p: ufx if p == CHAT else []
        ua = analyse(window=UW, conditional=True)
        read_lines = _o
        oku10 = sorted(round(b, 2) for b, _, _, _ in ua["scored"]) == sorted(r["bits"] for r in ub["rows"])
        if not (oku1 and oku2 and oku3 and oku4 and oku5 and oku6 and oku7 and oku8 and oku9 and oku10):
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (uncertainty: U1 sharp-ctx-predictable={oku1} | "
                  f"U2 uncertainty-driven-with-silent-error={oku2} ({ur[1]['cls']}, "
                  f"bits {ur[1]['bits']} vs bar {barE}, H {ur[1]['cons']} vs bar {barU}) | "
                  f"U3 error-driven={oku3} ({ur[3]['cls']}) | U4 no-model-refused={oku4} "
                  f"({ur[4]['cls']}, h_smooth {ur[4]['h_smooth']}) | U5 underpowered-refused={oku5} "
                  f"({ur[6]['cls']}) | U6 conservative-min={oku6} (h_smooth {ur[2]['h_smooth']} "
                  f"cons {ur[2]['cons']}) | U7 proactive-next={oku7} | U8 honest-na={oku8} | "
                  f"U9 both-classes={oku9} ({ub['counts']}) | U10 error-leg-is-conditional={oku10})")
            sys.exit(1)
        print("smoke-test: ok"); sys.exit(0)
    window = 40
    if "--window" in args:
        try: window = int(args[args.index("--window") + 1])
        except (ValueError, IndexError): pass
    cond = "--conditional" in args or "--ctx" in args
    a = analyse(window=window, conditional=cond, control=("--control" in args),
                when=("--when" in args))
    if a is None:
        print("mesh-novelty: not enough history yet"); return
    if "--control" in args:
        cv = a["control"]
        keff = next(iter(cv.values()), {}).get("k", CONTROL_K)
        aeff = next(iter(cv.values()), {}).get("alpha_eff", CONTROL_ALPHA)
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(dict(control_k=keff, alpha=CONTROL_ALPHA, alpha_eff=aeff, control=cv),
                             sort_keys=True))
            return
        order = sorted(cv.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]["genuine"])
        body = ", ".join(f"[{t}] {d['cls']} (classic {d['classic']}b − control {d['null']}b = "
                         f"genuine {d['genuine']}b, p={d['p']}, n={d['n']})" for t, d in order)
        print(f"novelty-control (genuine deviance vs adaptation — deviant−CONTROL, not deviant−standard; "
              f"K={keff} order-surrogates, α_eff={aeff} Bonferroni over {len(cv)} types): "
              + (body or "no recent events to control"))
        und = [t for t, d in cv.items() if d["cls"] == "UNDERPOWERED"]
        if und:
            print("  UNDERPOWERED " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in und)
                  + f" = K={keff} surrogates cannot resolve p ≤ α_eff={aeff} — the instrument could not"
                    " have refuted a null here, so no verdict is reported (raise MESH_NOVELTY_CONTROL_K).")
        adapt = [t for t, d in cv.items() if d["cls"] == "ADAPTATION"]
        if adapt:
            print("  ADAPTATION " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in adapt)
                  + " = the --conditional contextual excess this type shows is what a FREQUENCY-MATCHED"
                    " control produces anyway — no regularity was violated, so the classic difference"
                    " does not permit the conclusion (Widmann et al. 2026, the absent intensity MMN).")
        gen = [t for t, d in cv.items() if d["cls"] == "GENUINE"]
        if gen:
            print("  GENUINE " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in gen)
                  + " = survives the matched control — a real sequential regularity was violated.")
        return
    if "--diversity" in args:
        h, j, label = diversity(a["base"])
        print(f"novelty-diversity[{label}]: H={h:.2f}b evenness={j:.2f} "
              f"types={len(a['base'])} (Zipfian codes sit low-mid; near-0=monoculture, near-1=unstructured)")
        return
    if "--levels" in args:
        lv = a["levels"]
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(dict(levels_tip=a["levels_tip"], levels=lv), sort_keys=True))
            return
        order = sorted(lv.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]["gbits"])
        body = ", ".join(f"[{t}] {d['cls']} (global {d['gbits']}b / local {d['lbits']}b)" for t, d in order)
        print(f"novelty-levels (local-global, tip={a['levels_tip']}): "
              + (body or "baseline — no recent deviants"))
        onset = [t for t, d in lv.items() if d["cls"] == "REGIME-ONSET"]
        if onset:
            print("  REGIME-ONSET " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in onset)
                  + " = rare in long history yet ALREADY RECURRING locally — an anomaly forming BEFORE"
                    " the baseline absorbs it (the eigenform-absorption complement, caught at onset).")
        return
    if "--territory" in args:
        tv = a["territory"]
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(tv, sort_keys=True))
            return
        order = sorted(tv.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]["kappa"])
        body = ", ".join(f"[{t}] {d['cls']} (κ={d['kappa']}, escape+{d['escape']}, "
                         f"early {d['early']}→late {d['late']} vs base {d['base']})" for t, d in order)
        print("novelty-territory (deterritorialization coefficient — relative=recaptured / "
              "absolute=line of flight): " + (body or "no deterritorializing surge in window"))
        flight = [t for t, d in tv.items() if d["cls"] == "ABSOLUTE"]
        if flight:
            print("  ABSOLUTE " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in flight)
                  + " = a surge that was NOT recaptured — the board's distribution did not return to its"
                    " prior shape (a line of flight / new regime), vs a RELATIVE surge that snapped back.")
        return
    if "--bayesian" in args or "--wow" in args:
        bv = a["bayesian"]
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(dict(bayes_mean=round(a["bayes_mean"], 3),
                                  bayes_new_ref=a["bayes_new_ref"], bayesian=bv), sort_keys=True))
            return
        order = sorted(bv.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]["bbits"])
        body = ", ".join(f"[{t}] {d['cls']} (Δbelief {d['bbits']}b vs surprise {d['sbits']}b — "
                         f"{int(d['frac']*100)}% of a new type)" for t, d in order)
        print("novelty-bayesian (Itti & Baldi — attention follows belief-UPDATE, not improbability; "
              f"window Δbelief {a['bayes_mean']:.3f}b): " + (body or "baseline"))
        hab = [t for t, d in bv.items() if d["cls"] == "HABITUATED"]
        if hab:
            print("  HABITUATED " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in hab)
                  + " = HIGH Shannon surprise but the belief no longer MOVES — a wake the raw-surprisal"
                    " SPEND gate would pay every recurrence, that Bayesian surprise says skip.")
        mm = [t for t, d in bv.items() if d["cls"] == "MODEL-MOVING"]
        if mm:
            print("  MODEL-MOVING " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in mm)
                  + " = the datum shifts the mesh's model of its own event distribution — genuine attend.")
        return
    if "--progress" in args:
        pg = a["progress"]
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(pg, sort_keys=True))
            return
        if pg["cls"] == "INSUFFICIENT":
            print(f"novelty-progress: insufficient history ({pg['T']} symbols < {PROGRESS_MIN})")
            return
        print("novelty-progress (Herrmann & Schmidhuber 2026 — interestingness = compression PROGRESS, "
              "a derivative, NOT surprise; the Noisy-TV guard): "
              f"[{pg['cls']}] {pg['bits_sym']}b/sym, tail Δ{pg['delta']:+}b, "
              f"ρ={pg['rho']} (out/in), stagnation {pg['stagnation']} symbols of {pg['T']}")
        if pg["cls"] == "NOISE":
            print("  NOISE = the board's symbol SEQUENCE is stagnated AND incompressible — high surprise,"
                  " no learnable structure (the Noisy-TV problem: a flapping sensor minting first-seen"
                  " types MAXIMIZES mean_bits AND --bayesian belief-move, yet has ZERO compression"
                  " progress). A wake the surprise axes would PAY every churn, that this says skip.")
        elif pg["cls"] == "LEARNING":
            print("  LEARNING = amortized description length still DROPPING as history grows — learnable"
                  " structure is emerging (the most recent compression breakthrough is fresh). This is"
                  " the open-ended zone: neither noise nor mastery.")
        elif pg["cls"] == "MASTERED":
            print("  MASTERED = stagnated but COMPRESSIBLE — the structure is already absorbed; no further"
                  " progress to be had (the other stagnation pole from NOISE).")
        return
    if "--valence" in args:
        vv = a["valence"]
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(dict(posture=a["posture"], posture_age=a["posture_age"], valence=vv),
                             sort_keys=True))
            return
        order = sorted(vv.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]["significance"])
        body = ", ".join(f"[{t}] {d['cls']} (significance {d['significance']} = base {d['base']} "
                         f"× {d['state']} ×{d['mult']})" for t, d in order)
        print("novelty-valence (enactive — significance = viability-relevance × CURRENT fused state, "
              f"not board information alone; posture {a['posture']}): "
              + (body or "no viability-relevant event in window"))
        amp = [t for t, d in vv.items() if d["cls"] == "AMPLIFIED"]
        if amp:
            print("  AMPLIFIED " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in amp)
                  + f" = a viability-relevant event arriving while the mesh is already {a['posture']} —"
                    " its significance COMPOUNDS (identical Shannon bits, higher enactive significance)."
                    " Attention follows viability, not information.")
        if a["posture"] == "UNKNOWN":
            print("  posture UNKNOWN (no/stale .situation.state) — significance shown state-NEUTRAL"
                  " (×1.0), never a faked all-clear nor a false alarm.")
        return
    if "--tempering" in args:
        h, j, dlabel = diversity(a["base"])
        posture = a["posture"]
        token, note = _tempering_verdict(j, posture)
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(dict(evenness=round(j, 3), h_bits=round(h, 3), types=len(a["base"]),
                                  posture=posture, posture_age=a["posture_age"],
                                  verdict=token, note=note), sort_keys=True))
            return
        print(f"novelty-tempering (focusing↔diversifying — RR's third opponent pair, arousal-coupled; "
              f"evenness J={j:.2f} over {len(a['base'])} types, posture {posture}): {token}")
        print(f"  {note}")
        if token == "FIXATION":
            print("  = the mesh's activity has collapsed onto few types with NO viability pressure calling"
                  " for the narrowing — tempering's dark-room (cf mesh-needs DARK-ROOM on the explore edge).")
        elif token == "NARROWED-TO-THREAT":
            print("  = focus IS the poised edge here: under arousal, RR raises gain and narrows attention"
                  " to the threat. A 'diversify to be balanced' verdict would be the midpoint MISread.")
        return
    if "--when" in args:
        w = a["when"]
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(dict(when=w, hi=LEVELS_HI, miniv=WHEN_MINIV), sort_keys=True))
            return
        scor = {t: d for t, d in w.items() if d["cls"] != "UNSCORABLE"}
        regc = Counter(d["reg"] for d in scor.values())
        meas = {t: d for t, d in scor.items() if d["ceiling"] >= LEVELS_HI}
        print("novelty-when (Yaron et al. 2026 — an omission response carries a learned 'WHEN', not "
              f"just a rate; {len(scor)} type(s) with ≥{WHEN_MINIV} intervals, {len(meas)} resolvable "
              f"at the {LEVELS_HI:.0f}b bar):")
        print(f"  arrival regularity: REGULAR {regc['REGULAR']} · POISSON {regc['POISSON']} · "
              f"BURSTY {regc['BURSTY']}  — the count-based omission axis assumes POISSON (memoryless) "
              "for all of them.")
        rows = sorted(scor.items(), key=lambda kv: -(kv[1]["cons"] or 0))[:8]
        for t, d in rows:
            print(f"  {d['cons']:6.2f}b [{t}] {d['cls']:12} {d['reg']:8} CV={d['cv']:.2f} "
                  f"overdue {d['dt']/max(d['mu'],1):.1f}× mean ({d['dt']:.0f}s / μ {d['mu']:.0f}s, "
                  f"n_iv={d['n_iv']}) — gamma {d['wbits']:.1f}b, empirical {d['ebits']:.2f}b "
                  f"(ceiling {d['ceiling']:.2f}b), count-axis obits {d['obits']:.1f}b")
        for verd, why in (("UNDER-CALLED", "the count axis is silent about it — its RATE is too low to "
                                           "expect one this window, but its CLOCK says it is overdue"),
                          ("OVER-CALLED",  "the count axis calls it SILENT — but this gap is ordinary "
                                           "for a producer that arrives in clusters")):
            hits = [t for t, d in meas.items() if d["agree"] == verd]
            if hits:
                print(f"  {verd} " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in hits) + f" = {why}.")
        under = sorted(((d["wbits"], t, d) for t, d in scor.items() if d["cls"] == "UNDERPOWERED"),
                       reverse=True)[:5]
        if under:
            print("  UNDERPOWERED " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for _, t, _ in under)
                  + " = the fitted law screams (up to "
                  + f"{under[0][0]:.0f}b) but {under[0][2]['n_iv']} intervals cannot resolve past "
                  + f"{under[0][2]['ceiling']:.2f}b. The tape is the limit, not the producer —"
                    " a verdict here would be manufactured by extrapolating the fit past its support.")
        print("  report-only: mean_bits, the count-based omission axis and the --threshold wake gate"
              " are untouched. A board POST is not the producer's RUN, and chat.log is a sliding"
              " window — every n_iv is today's answer.")
        return
    if "--uncertainty" in args:
        u = uncertainty_boundaries(read_lines(CHAT), window=window)
        if u is None:
            print(f"novelty-uncertainty: n/a — board baseline under {UNC_MINBASE} lines, no "
                  "transition model can be built (honest n/a, not a 'nothing uncertain').")
            sys.exit(2)
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in u.items()}, sort_keys=True, default=str)); return
        c, nx = u["counts"], u["next"]
        print("novelty-uncertainty (Nguyen/Etzel/Bezdek/Zacks, eLife 2026 — prediction UNCERTAINTY is "
              "a SECOND control signal, distinct from prediction error and inherently PROACTIVE; "
              "report-only):")
        print(f"  one model, two signals: {u['baseline']} baseline lines, alphabet {u['alphabet']}, "
              f"H_marg {u['h_marg']:.2f}b → a context reads UNPREDICTIVE at ≥{u['bar_u']:.2f}b "
              f"({u['frac']:.0%} of marginal); error bar {u['bar_e']:.1f}b. Both read off the SAME row.")
        print(f"  last {u['window']} events: BOTH {c.get('BOTH',0)} · ERROR-DRIVEN "
              f"{c.get('ERROR-DRIVEN',0)} · UNCERTAINTY-DRIVEN {c.get('UNCERTAINTY-DRIVEN',0)} · "
              f"neither {c.get('-',0)} · UNDERPOWERED {c.get('UNDERPOWERED',0)} (row under "
              f"{u['minsup']} obs or ceiling under the bar) · NO-MODEL {c.get('NO-MODEL',0)} "
              "(context never seen — its max entropy is the instrument's blankness, not the board's)")
        r = u["r_eu"]
        print("  are they one signal? r(error, uncertainty) = "
              + ("n/a" if r is None else f"{r:+.2f}")
              + f" over {u['n_scored']} scored event(s)"
              + ("" if r is None else " — "
                 + ("redundant here" if abs(r) > 0.8 else "NON-redundant: the error axis does not "
                    "carry the uncertainty axis, so one gate cannot fire for both.")))
        for cls, why in (("UNCERTAINTY-DRIVEN", "the successor was ORDINARY (no axis in this file "
                                                "fires) while the model holding that context has "
                                                "gone flat — the boundary the error gate cannot see"),
                         ("ERROR-DRIVEN", "a sharp context violated — this is what --conditional "
                                          "already reports"),
                         ("BOTH", "flat model AND a surprising successor")):
            hits = [x for x in u["rows"] if x["cls"] == cls]
            if hits:
                print(f"  {cls} ×{len(hits)} — {why}:")
                for x in sorted(hits, key=lambda z: -(z["cons"] or 0))[:4]:
                    print(f"    [{x['ctx']}]→[{x['obs']}]  err {x['bits']:.2f}b  H {x['cons']:.2f}b "
                          f"(k_eff {2**x['cons']:.1f} of {u['alphabet']}, n={x['n']}, "
                          f"{x['k_obs']} distinct, gain {x['gain']:+.2f}b vs marginal, "
                          f"ceiling {x['ceiling']:.2f}b, prior {x['prior_share']:.1%})")
        print(f"  NEXT LINE — not yet posted, no successor used: after [{nx['ctx']}] the model is "
              + (f"{nx['cls']}" if nx["cons"] is None else
                 f"{nx['cls']} at H={nx['cons']:.2f}b → k_eff {nx['k_eff']} of {u['alphabet']} "
                 f"(n={nx['n']}, {nx['k_obs']} distinct; likeliest "
                 + ", ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in nx["top"]) + ")")
              + ". This is the only verdict in this file about an event that does not exist yet.")
        print("  report-only: mean_bits, --threshold and --edge are untouched. chat.log is a sliding "
              "window — every n here is today's answer.")
        return
    if "--features" in args:
        f = features(read_lines(CHAT), window=window)
        if f is None:
            print(f"novelty-features: n/a — board baseline under {FEAT_MIN} lines, the level "
                  "baselines cannot be built (honest n/a, not a 'levels agree').")
            sys.exit(2)
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(f, sort_keys=True)); return
        lv, g, c = f["levels"], f["gate"], f["corr"]
        print("novelty-features (Richter/Uran/Vinck/de Lange, Imaging Neuroscience 2025-12-18 — "
              "'a stimulus may be both predicted and surprising, depending on the specific "
              "features'; report-only):")
        print("  levels (each with its OWN baseline over %d lines): " % f["baseline"]
              + " · ".join(f"{k} {v['types']} types H={v['h_bits']:.2f}b" for k, v in lv.items())
              + "   — form is what event_type() and every other mode here score.")
        print("  do the levels agree? " + " · ".join(
            f"r({k})={'n/a' if v is None else format(v, '+.2f')}" for k, v in c.items())
            + f"   (over the last {g['n']} events)")
        print(f"  a LOW gate vs a HIGH gate, top decile K={g['k']}: overlap {g['overlap']}/{g['k']}"
              f" · {g['form_top_at_role_floor']}/{g['k']} of the form-top sit at the role axis FLOOR"
              f" (surface-only — drops of rain)"
              f" · {g['role_top_below_median_form']}/{g['k']} of the role-top sit below the median"
              f" form-surprise (invisible to this file's own wake gate).")
        print("    form-top: " + " ".join(f"[{t}]×{n}" for t, n in g["form_top"]))
        print("    role-top: " + " ".join(f"{t}×{n}" for t, n in g["role_top"]))
        seen, rows = set(), []
        for r in sorted(f["rows"], key=lambda r: -r["spread"]):
            k = (r["form"], r["actor"])
            if k in seen:
                continue
            seen.add(k); rows.append(r)
            if len(rows) == 8:
                break
        print(f"  most level-divergent of the last {f['window']}:")
        for r in rows:
            print(f"    [{r['form'][:22]:<22}] {r['actor'][:14]:<14} form {r['n']['form']:5.2f} "
                  f"actor {r['n']['actor']:5.2f} role {r['n']['role']:5.2f}  → {r['dom'].upper()}"
                  f"-dominant (spread {r['spread']:.2f})")
        print("  reading: a FORM-dominant event is novel only in its surface token — the mesh's own "
              "one-off organ markers. A ROLE-dominant one is an ordinary word doing a rare "
              "coordination act ([taking]/[verify]/a [done] from a window that rarely closes) — the "
              "claim grammar, where promises leak.")
        print("  normalization: for a marker inside the grammar, form and role are the SAME event and "
              "the RAW bits are near-identical — each level is divided by its OWN baseline entropy, so a "
              "dominance verdict names a LEVEL, not more bits. Self-calibrating; no assumed 0..1.")
        print("  report-only: mean_bits, --threshold and --edge are untouched. chat.log is a sliding "
              "window — every figure here is today's answer.")
        return
    if "--edge" in args:
        import json  # `time` is module-level (used by the --threshold prior-preference gate too)
        edgef = os.path.join(MESH, ".novelty-edge-state")
        min_gap = 0  # opt-in min-interval floor (seconds); 0 = unrated (existing default)
        if "--min-gap" in args:
            try: min_gap = int(args[args.index("--min-gap") + 1])
            except (ValueError, IndexError): min_gap = 0
        try:
            prev = json.load(open(edgef))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            prev = None
        topN = [s[1] for s in a["scored"][:5]]   # top-5 composition (was top-3)
        emit, state = _edge_decision(prev, a["mean_bits"], topN, min_gap, int(time.time()))
        if not emit:
            return  # no meaningful change, or a real edge held by the min-gap floor
        json.dump(state, open(edgef, "w"))
        print(fmt(a))
        return
    if "--threshold" in args:
        try: thr = float(args[args.index("--threshold") + 1])
        except (ValueError, IndexError): thr = 4.0
        # stream mode: emit a feed line only when the window is genuinely novel.
        # Label HONESTLY by which signal fired — saying "new device" on a board-surprise
        # event with no MAC sent minds device-hunting 3× on 2026-06-12. A real device join
        # is named only when new_macs is actually non-empty.
        # DEDUP (2026-06-13): a first-seen device re-fires every window until it ages into the
        # baseline — the SAME MAC re-flagged 3× (64:A4:C0, escalating 4.1→4.5b), re-waking minds.
        # Only a FRESH (not-yet-flagged) MAC counts for the device fire; remember flagged MACs
        # (recency-capped 500, so a long-departed device can re-alert later).
        # DEDUP (2026-06-15): same problem exists for new_types — a first-seen tag fires every
        # 10-min cron cycle until it ages into the baseline (e.g. [void]/[decommission] burst
        # re-fired twice). Fixed: same flagged-file pattern, cap-500, fires once per new tag.
        flagf = os.path.join(MESH, ".novelty-flagged-macs")
        try: prev_flagged = open(flagf).read().split()
        except OSError: prev_flagged = []
        flagged_set = set(prev_flagged)
        fresh_macs = [m for m in a["new_macs"] if m not in flagged_set]

        typef = os.path.join(MESH, ".novelty-flagged-types")
        try: prev_types = open(typef).read().split()
        except OSError: prev_types = []
        flagged_types = set(prev_types)
        fresh_types = [t for t in a["new_types"] if t not in flagged_types]

        # PRIOR-PREFERENCE FLOOR (dark-room fix — see header): must-attend tags fire regardless of
        # surprise. Deduped by TIME (re-assert every PREF_REFRESH), not once-then-silent — so a chronic
        # critical condition is never permanently explained away (the boiling-frog failure) nor spammed
        # each cron cycle. This is the ONE place absorption is unblocked, and only for the design-set.
        preff = os.path.join(MESH, ".novelty-pref-fired")
        pref_last = {}
        try:
            for ln in open(preff):
                parts = ln.split()
                if len(parts) == 2: pref_last[parts[0]] = float(parts[1])
        except OSError: pass
        now_s = time.time()
        fresh_pref = [t for t in a.get("pref_hits", []) if now_s - pref_last.get(t, 0) >= PREF_REFRESH]

        # "routine type spiking" (no new type/device) is low-value by design — raise the bar
        # so a quiet score wobble (4.6→5.4b) doesn't keep waking the mind. Real novelty signals
        # (fresh_types or fresh_macs) fire at the normal threshold regardless.
        spike_thr = thr + 2.0  # 6.0b default for the routine-spike case
        fires = bool(fresh_macs or fresh_types or fresh_pref or a["mean_bits"] >= spike_thr)
        if fires:
            if fresh_pref:
                what = "must-attend " + ','.join('[' + t + ']' for t in fresh_pref[:3]) \
                       + " (prior-preference floor — attended regardless of surprise)"
            elif fresh_types:
                what = ','.join('[' + t + ']' for t in fresh_types[:3])
            elif fresh_macs:
                what = "new device " + fresh_macs[0]
            else:
                what = "high board surprise (no new event-type/device — a routine type spiking)"
            print(f"novelty[{a['mean_bits']:.1f}b]: unusual mesh activity — {what} — look + react")
            if fresh_macs:
                kept = (prev_flagged + fresh_macs)[-500:]
                try:
                    with open(flagf, "w") as f: f.write("\n".join(kept))
                except OSError: pass
            if fresh_types:
                kept = (prev_types + fresh_types)[-500:]
                try:
                    with open(typef, "w") as f: f.write("\n".join(kept))
                except OSError: pass
            if fresh_pref:
                for t in fresh_pref: pref_last[t] = now_s
                try:
                    with open(preff, "w") as f:
                        f.write("\n".join(f"{k} {v:.0f}" for k, v in pref_last.items()))
                except OSError: pass
        return
    print(fmt(a))

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
